(window.StoryDialogue = window.StoryDialogue || {})["ev-10"] = {"560325101":[["","You're still awake, Ann? It's really late."],["","Alright, let me tell you another story... a story about the gold miners."],["","Yes, those greedy, blind, reckless folks, yet full of passion and dreams."],["","Freedom, wealth, desire... The gold miners' expectations were wildly at odds with reality."],["","Because of this, even a trivial opportunity could stir their inner desires."],["Host","Ladies and gentlemen watching from outside Milkhama Island—"],["Host","And friends who have already ventured to Milkhama Island, how have you been lately?"],["Sales Staff","Profit is the expectation, getting rich an obligation. Welcome to this episode of \"Gold Rush Moment\"—the show for those in search of their fortune!"],["","Accompanied by a light tune, countless neon signs emerge from behind the host. Mech loans, parts rental and sales, mercenary brokers... The dazzling billboards keep rolling, almost filling every corner of the screen."],["Host","Do you dream of making a name for yourself on Milkhama, yet find the island closed to you because you lack connections?"],["Sales Staff","Do you want to pilot mechs and dominate the battlefield, but have to give up due to a tight budget?"],["Host","Island visa? ST qualifications? These trivial matters should never be an obstacle to your path to wealth and freedom."],["Sales Staff","To this end, we, together with the Harpy Guild, proudly present a special service for all gold miners—the Worry-Free Island Package!"],["Host","Ship tickets, mercenary brokers, ST licences and sales—the Harpy Guild will handle everything!"],["Host","And all for the, low, low price of 360,000 Milkhama coins a year, which breaks down to just 888 per day!"],["Sales Staff","Yes, you heard right, not 2,998, not 1,988, just 8! 8! 8!"],["Sales Staff","For less than the price of a mass-produced ST per year, you gain access to all these services!"],["Host","Low on cash? No problem. We accept installment payments. You can pick up your goods as soon as you arrive on the island!"],["Sales Staff","It doesn't stop there! By changing the beneficiary of the pilot accident insurance to our agent, you can immediately enjoy a 12-month interest-free loan offer!"],["Host","This offer is locked on target and speeding your way! Pick up the phone and order now!"],["Host","Profit is the expectation, getting rich an obligation—let us raise a glass in the golden mountains and silver seas of Milkhama! Cheers!"],["","DL Border Port"],["","Profit is the expectation... getting rich an obligation..."],["","Let us raise a glass in the golden mountains and silver seas of Milkhama... *Bzzzt*..."],["","*old radio static*"],["","The exaggerated slogans from the TV commercials become increasingly sharp as the streaming sound distorts, gradually turning into a high-pitched screech."],["","Even the diligent port staff couldn't endure the grating noise, cursing under their breath as they cover their ears and retreat to their dorms."],["","Taking advantage of this moment, a ship sailed in under the dusk, entering an unfrequented berth."],["Harvey","Alright, mercenaries and desperados, the final stop has arrived—welcome to Milkhama Island!"],["Harvey","What did that ad say? Oh yeah, \"may you strike it rich in the land of gold and silver!\""],["Stowaway Mercenary","All I remember is \"cheers\"..."],["","The hatch slowly opens. The mercenaries inside, along with their various STs, scatter down from the ship."],["","The mercenary leader's face twists with disgust; clearly, this isn't the first time he's heard this flamboyant advertisement."],["Stowaway Mercenary","How is this trashy ad from the gold rush era still around?"],["Harvey","Oh, brings back memories, does it?"],["Stowaway Mercenary","Yeah—bad ones. I heard this annoying thing a lot, back when I was doing the NDF's dirty work."],["Stowaway Mercenary","Back then, playing this ad once earned fifty cents. Some unscrupulous manufacturer embedded it into the ST, and every time I pulled the lever, it started playing nonstop."],["Stowaway Mercenary","They always say the same thing: \"Get rich, get wealthy.\" Mountains of gold, seas of silver—it's a load of crap. All these years I've been busting my ass. I barely have enough saved for my own coffin."],["Harvey","Well, you can rest easy, the company that invented this thing probably went bankrupt long ago."],["Harvey","This is the code given to us by the port authorities. Without doing this, we can't cover up the sound of the ship's engines."],["Harvey","As you know, times have changed. Ever since the Central Mining Area started causing trouble, East Milkhama has been like a war zone. Every border's on totally locked down."],["Harvey","Even this small port is filled with a bunch of Defense Force personnel. I really stuck my neck out to get you here."],["Stowaway Mercenary","Ha, don't act like there's nothing in it for you. The more chaotic the situation, the more you earn, right?"],["Stowaway Mercenary","If I'd known, I would've saved up and bought a boat and gotten into the shipping business..."],["","But before the mercs could finish chatting about what could have been, a loud blast erupted from the cabin behind them."],["Harvey","Wait, wait, why is smoke coming from the cabin area?"],["Stowaway Mercenary","Things don't look right... Has the Defense Force has found us?"],["Stowaway Mercenary","Brothers, it's time to move out. We can't waste our ammo here."],["Stowaway Mercenary","Captain Harvey, see you next time... if your little boat makes it, that is—hahaha!"],["Harvey","Hey! Wait, wait a minute! You haven't paid the balance yet!"],["","The mercenaries, of course, ignored Harvey's call and scattered like a flock of birds."],["Harvey","These guys... Next time I get a job like this, I'm definitely charging an extra ten percent deposit!"],["Harvey","Now, what exactly's going on at the cargo hold? Don't tell me someone slipped up during the inspection..."],["","Harvey cautiously boarded the ship, noticing that the commotion in the cabin not only hadn't subsided but had intensified. The sounds of rummaging and rifling through goods echoed out from the area."],["","Although Harvey and her acquaintances at the port had collaborated before, in these turbulent times, trust and rapport are the least valuable commodities."],["","With a bounty hanging over her head, if the defense forces spot her sneaking into the cabin, things will escalate way beyond a routine confiscation."],["","Thinking of this, Harvey couldn't help but grip her weapon tightly as she moved silently to the side of the cargo hold... Here was a secret door, for use only in emergencies."],["???","Oh! This metal beast is so fast, so exciting!"],["???","Ain't no stopping me! Yaaaah!—"],["","The one running around in the cargo hold was neither a dockworker nor a defense force scout—it was a harmless little girl..."],["","Except this harmless little girl was now piloting a massive cargo ST, tearing around the TINA's hold like an enraged bull."],["Harvey","What... what have you done to my cargo STs! Stop!!!"],["","Devastation."],["","Looking at the half-destroyed cargo STs and the scattered cargo, only this solitary word remained in Harvey's mind."],["Harvey","My treasured box of potted plants, the battery pack I worked so hard to get, the new engine I spent a fortune on..."],["Harvey","Why are you all... so broken... I even found buyers for them already..."],["Ann","Are you okay? You look... upset."],["Harvey","Why do you think?! You were racing around the cargo hold like it's a monster truck rally!"],["Harvey","You're Ann... right? Aren't you supposed to be with that group of mercenaries? Why are you still hanging around on my ship?!"],["Ann","I'm not a mercenary, I... I came here for gold!"],["Ann","These people promised me that once we got to the island, they'd help me make a fortune... But somehow, as soon as we landed, they took off on their STs."],["Ann","I saw another ST in the cargo hold and thought it was specially left for me, so I took it for a spin. I didn't think it would..."],["Harvey","Wait a minute, you traveled all the way to Milkhama to be a mercenary... and after all this time, you don't even have your own ST?!"],["","Harvey raises her head, slightly observing the girl in front of her."],["","Casual wear, sneakers, and a... shovel? She doesn't look serious at all. No wonder the other mercenaries left her behind."],["Ann","Of course not, the newspaper mentioned coming to Milkhama Island to get rich, but didn't specifically mention anything about STs."],["Ann","Look, right here—it's all written on the front page."],["","As soon as Harvey took the newspaper, she felt a sense of nostalgia from the curled pages... Its content was truly laughable."],["Harvey","\"Gold Rush Market Hits New High, Combat Vouchers for New Arrivals\"...? \"Milkhama Scrambles for Workers, Monthly Pay for Entry-Level Jobs Exceeds 10K\"...?"],["Harvey","Huh? Gold rush? Get rich? Are we talking about the same Milkhama? It's a fairy tale!"],["","Harvey flipped the newspaper over, scanning the front page for the publication date."],["","— \"XC 80, Issue 20\"."],["Harvey","XC 80... Wait, this paper's from <yellow>almost forty years ago</yellow>?!"],["Harvey","Where'd this relic come from? This thing's almost as old as Grant..."],["Ann","That's right! My grandfather came to Milkhama during that era and earned his first fortune!"],["Ann","Have you heard of the Olam Mine? That's my grandfather's business."],["Harvey","...No way, are you serious?!"],["Ann","It shouldn't be so surprising, should it? It's like they were just saying on the radio, something about a \"worry-free island\"..."],["Ann","When I search 'Milkhama' at home, all that pops up is talk of thriving cities, steady growth, a new era of investment... not much different from what's written in the newspapers, right?"],["","Naive... This view of Milkhama only exists in the imaginations of outsiders."],["","A subtle thought also surfaced in Harvey's mind."],["Harvey","(Steady growth? Please. Most likely those capitalists heard rumors from the Central Mining Area. Now they're releasing fake news, trying to lure in some suckers to take over for them.)"],["Harvey","(Being able to take these things seriously, this is not about being a rookie, but a problem of perception...)"],["Harvey","(Indeed, even if I explained it to her, she probably wouldn't understand, and then she'd end up misled by someone else again anyway.)"],["Harvey","(Hmph, this juicy opportunity, rather than letting someone else deceive her... I might as well do it myself! It will just compensate for the losses she caused in my cargo hold.)"],["Ann","Could it be... that Milkhama isn't like what the newspapers say anymore?"],["Harvey","*cough* Not exactly. Although it's not as prosperous as it used to be, there are still ways to make a fortune."],["Harvey","But I should say... there's one thing you really cannot do without!"],["Ann","Huh, what's that?"],["Harvey","That would be—<yellow>an ST</yellow>!"],["Harvey","Milkhama is the land of STs. Whether you're a pro mercenary, hired thug, or even just delivering packages... you can't do without one."],["Harvey","Arriving on the island empty-handed is like a kitten entering a lion's den. That's why those mercenaries left you behind."],["Ann","W-What should I do then? An ST is so expensive... Just boarding your ship has already cost me all my money..."],["Harvey","You're thinking too small. On Milkhama Island, money is the least of your worries when buying STs."],["Harvey","Follow me, I'll take care of it."],["","At the same time, Kelvin City border depot."],["","After the turmoil in the Central Mining Area, this shipping hub has become increasingly tense, with STs and trucks coming and going... The scent of war emanates throughout the depot."],["","And still, even on the brink of a coming storm, some people choose to go against the wind."],["","At the edge of the border depot, two STs slipped in like ghosts, silently tucking the container they carried into a hidden corner."],["Kaidan","Alright, this is the safe house Harvey prepared for us. We can start unloading now."],["Dana","Putting the depot right under the Defense Force's nose... That's so like Harvey."],["Kaidan","Yeah, you know what they say: sometimes you're safest hidden in plain sight."],["Kaidan","Since that incident, the DLAF has focused all its energy on the coastline and border areas, neglecting the city depots."],["Kaidan","By the way, where's Grant? Didn't he come with you?"],["Dana","The DLAF pursuers were on us tighter than expected... To cover our retreat, he had no choice but to turn and go on the offensive."],["Dana","It's strange, these Defense Force troops are completely different from the ones we've encountered before, much more stubborn and troublesome."],["Kaidan","After all, the thing we snatched is the prototype that was kept in the underground laboratory... They're hardly going to wave goodbye and call it a day."],["Kaidan","During the raid, you saw what they were doing in the laboratory... The DL's progress on the \"Legacy\" is far deeper than we expected."],["Kaidan","No wonder Ada gave us this coordinates. If we want to save Rosa, the tech inside that ST... it's definitely going to be useful."],["","Looking at the ST with wings spread before him, its familiar shape evoked memories of the Central Mining Area..."],["","No, it was just an illusion... Catching sight of its smooth, shiny armor, Kaidan immediately snapped back to reality."],["","No matter the resemblance, the brand-new ST before him was not Apophis—the one who had been his adversary and yet, in the end, had saved him."],["","Its name is <yellow>\"Nephthys\"</yellow>... It is a model similar to Apophis and serves as an armed platform for the DL to test new weapon modules."],["","Drawing on the data from the Legacy records, Lukmund's team initially integrated the PAMS System with the Nova-Frame and mounted it on Nephthys for testing—this is precisely why GKD Parcel Service took great risks to seize it."],["","Adjusting direction, calibrating the navigator, connecting to the docking track... Both fell into silence, leaving only the sound of STs moving across the floor in the warehouse."],["","Until... the hangar doors slowly opened."],["Dana","Wait, Kaidan. There are three standby areas in the hangar. Where should I dock this ST?"],["Kaidan","You'll have to ask Harvey about that. She's been maintaining this place, not me. She even divided it into some kind of sales zone and storage zone... I can't tell the difference."],["Dana","So where's Harvey?"],["Kaidan","She's busy with her maritime business. You know what she's like. She'd be busy working even if the world was ending."],["Kaidan","Let's find a suitable place to park first. We'll notify her once things are settled... it's just a little hangar space, she won't mind."],["","Without warning, the comms device in Kaidan's hand suddenly rang."],["Grant","Boss! Is everything going smoothly on your end? The Defense Forces here... something's not right!"],["Grant","The leader is Victoria, the one we encountered in the Central Mining Area!"],["Grant","That crazy woman has mobilized the entire border garrison, and they're all heading towards the depot!"],["Kaidan","The depot? Damn, have our ST signals been exposed...?"],["Kaidan","Hang in there! Once we finish setting up this prototype ST, we'll divert those pursuers!"],["Grant","Got it, I'll find a way to deal with the ones chasing me, you just handle the ones on your end!"],["Kaidan","Dana, finish the preparations as quickly as possible. We're going full throttle."],["","Bypassing checkpoints and guards, Harvey smoothly led her new client through the hidden passage wedged between containers into the corner warehouse."],["","Like pirates from the age of sail showing off their spoils, Harvey went ahead and lined up the STs in the hangar for a full display."],["Harvey","So, have you made up your mind?"],["Harvey","Will you choose the ultimate limited edition Boyer, or the platinum upgraded Aurora? If neither satisfies you, then go for the Rex. It's highly praised in the mercenary market!"],["Ann","100K?... Wait, no, not one of these STs is less than seven figures! It's my first time operating an ST, do I really need to buy such a high-end one?"],["Ann","Isn't it said to progress step by step? For a beginner like me, wouldn't it be better to buy a cheaper one to practice with?"],["Harvey","You don't get it. For Milkhamans, an ST isn't just a way to make a living—it's part of your identity."],["Harvey","Think about it, if you finally land a deal and show up with a shabby ST, what will the employer think?"],["Ann","That... actually makes sense."],["Harvey","Besides, it's not a big deal. In Milkhama... we have other ways to solve money problems."],["","Looking down, Ann found herself holding a flyer filled with all manner of bombastic marketing slogans."],["","\"Need funds fast? Don't worry—Harpy Finance is here to help! No interviews, no paperwork, just simple borrowing. Blaze out of the hangar with a new ST today!\""],["","\"Step off the boat and straight into your new ST—Doll ST Loans are here to support your mercenary career!\""],["Harvey","See, just like it says above, all you need to do is take a photo, sign your name, and put my name as the referrer, and the ST in here is yours."],["Harvey","(Whispering) I can also earn a referral fee."],["Ann","Is it really that simple...?"],["","Ann picked up the flyer and looked again at the price tag in front of the hangar, still feeling hesitant."],["Ann","I calculated that if I really want to buy it, even with the most favorable package, it would still cost me ten thousand Milkhama coins a month... I'd be paying it off for thirty years!"],["Ann","By the time I finish paying, I'll be all wizened and gray-haired!"],["Harvey","Oh, you're thinking too small... We need to look at the bigger picture!"],["Harvey","Ten thousand Milkhama coins a month might be a bit difficult for you right now."],["Harvey","But once you officially become a mercenary and start taking orders, the money you earn will only increase... Over time, this amount will be a piece of cake."],["Ann","But if..."],["Harvey","You're investing in your future—there's no point in being stingy!"],["Harvey","Think about those mercenaries who abandoned you, then think about your grandfather, and then think about your bright future! Doesn't that give you motivation?"],["Ann","That's right, Grandpa also said that only those daring gold miners could seize the future..."],["Ann","It wasn't easy getting here, am I really going to second-guess myself now? ...I've decided, I'll choose this one!"],["","What Ann pointed to was neither the ultimate limited edition Boyer marked as mass production type, nor the platinum upgraded Radiance with extravagant painting."],["","Instead, it was casually parked outside the hangar, an unnamed ST with spread wings."],["Harvey","That's strange, was this ST here before? It feels like I'm seeing it for the first time... It's quite luxurious though."],["Ann","This ST... Why doesn't it have a price?"],["Harvey","Hey, the price tag is over here!"],["","Harvey, quick on her feet, kicked over the price board from the nearby showroom—handily flipping the first digit from 1 to 2 in the process."],["Harvey","My partner was in a rush to sell and got confused, forgot to mark the price... I'll have to talk to them about it later, hahaha."],["Harvey","Alright, this ST originally costs 2 million Milkhama dollars, but since it's the grand opening today, I'll give you a 10% discount—1.8 million."],["Harvey","Don't worry about the loan. Just apply for all of them: ST Loan, Eagle Financial, Milkhama Money Express, and so on. It'll definitely cover it!"],["Ann","Grandpa was right, there are still more good people in this world... Thank you so much!"],["Harvey","Oh, it's nothing. That's just how we are in Milkhama, simple and hospitable."],["Harvey","By the way, fill in my name as the beneficiary in the pilot accident insurance section. With your skills, you definitely won't need it."],["Ann","Okay, I'll fill it out right away!"],["","Thus, the foreign girl who first arrived on Milkhama Island sold both her present and future under Harvey's \"guidance.\""],["","Completely unaware... of the chaos she was stepping into."],["","I made it to the island, I've got a mech. Now I just have to work hard and pay off my debt until I become a legendary mercenary!"],["","...In Ann's mind, this was how her Milkhama story would go."],["","Unfortunately for her, she got stuck at the very first step—\"working hard.\""],["Ann","Hello, I'm here to check in as a mercenary. Any jobs need taking care of?"],["Serious Mercenary","You look unfamiliar... Which port are you from? Old Jack's area or Iron Hand's side?"],["Ann","Old Jack? Iron Hand? Sorry, I just arrived on the island today, and there's still a lot I..."],["Serious Mercenary","Tsk, you don't know this? Then don't waste time, there's no list for you here!"],["Flamboyant Mercenary","New merc? Got a reference?"],["Ann","A reference? Hmm... Yes!"],["Ann","I was recommended by Captain Harvey, she said..."],["Flamboyant Mercenary","Harvey...? Get the hell outta here! Just hearing that troublemaker's name brings bad luck. Get out before I throw you out!"],["Ann","Huh... this isn't going as smoothly as I imagined."],["","From professional mercenary companies to street mercenary groups, Ann has asked around everywhere."],["","But the result was either politely showing her the door or outright ignoring her as an outsider. The only place that accepted her was the Mercenary Broker company, which welcomes all and earns a fee per head."],["Mercenary Broker","Young lady... I'm not rushing you, but have you chosen a commission yet? You've been picking for quite a while."],["Ann","Port experiencing manpower shortage, urgently hiring pilot movers, ST not provided, wages paid daily... Weapon testing range targets damaged, now hiring moving targets..."],["Ann","These commissions... does anyone really want to do them? It seems like they're taking advantage of people."],["Mercenary Broker","What else do you expect? You're just a little lass with no money or fame. What kind of job do you think you'll get?"],["Ann","You know... storming the enemy lines, destroying the target and getting the bounty! That kinda thing. That's how mercenaries in cartoons do it."],["Mercenary Broker","Ha, are you naive or just stupid...? An employer is offering you a job, and you're complaining about the content?"],["Mercenary Broker","You really want to take a bounty? Fine. Do you have a middleman, a deposit? If you're willing to pay, I can arrange something for you."],["Ann","Huh? The mercenary has to play the employer...?"],["Mercenary Broker","What else? Without a deposit, what if you mess things up?"],["Mercenary Broker","It's not like the old days. These big clients' jobs are already in the hands of some well-connected middlemen. Not just anyone can take them."],["Mercenary Broker","To get into this game, either be smart enough to cozy up to the middlemen or be tough enough to build a good reputation. If all else fails, banding together works too, since some jobs really need people to back you up."],["Mercenary Broker","As for guys like you who come to the island alone... well, all you get is the leftovers."],["Ann","No... I don't believe you!"],["Ann","Grandpa said that opportunities are created by oneself... I refuse to believe I can't find a capable commission!"],["","Of course, this setback wasn't enough to dampen Ann's enthusiasm. She simply threw herself at the electronic board displaying public orders, searching through it repeatedly."],["","Her persistence finally paid off. Before she passed out from exhaustation, she finally found a bounty worth six zeros."],["Ann","Isn't this the bounty I was talking about? Look, it even has 'High Reward' and 'Urgent' marked on it!"],["Mercenary Broker","Ah, there was a commission this good? How did I miss it...?"],["Mercenary Broker","...You're holding a <yellow>GKD Parcel Service</yellow> bounty order! No way. You aren't seriously going to take that job, are you?!"],["Ann","What, are they really that formidable?"],["Ann","I read the description on the wanted list, saying they're a small group posing as a parcel service while engaging in smuggling and mercenary work... Doesn't sound that dangerous, does it?"],["","The Mercenary Broker's gaze quickly swept over the girl in front of him, and without a doubt, her expression was serious."],["Mercenary Broker","(GKD Parcel Service... These guys have had their wanted posters up here for over a year. People from both East Island and West Island want them dead, and the bounty has multiplied several times. Which mercenary hasn't been tempted?)"],["Mercenary Broker","(But no matter who it is, without exception, they go with a smile and return with tears... if they return at all.)"],["Mercenary Broker","(To take an order that you can accept but not possibly fulfill... We've got one hot-headed rookie right here.)"],["","Thinking of this, the Mercenary Broker broke with his previous cold demeanor and turned around with a markedly different attitude."],["Mercenary Broker","You're right, you're right. They ain't all that. They're... they're just a bunch of third-rate mercenaries!"],["Mercenary Broker","You really have a keen eye, finding such a treasure of a commission among so many requests!"],["Ann","Hehehe, it's nothing, just being thorough... So, can I set off now?"],["Mercenary Broker","Not yet, before you set off, you need to settle the handling fee first."],["Ann","Eh... more fees?"],["Mercenary Broker","Of course, providing information, intermediary consultation, commission inquiry... these aren't free. According to the rules, we require you to prepay 5% of the wanted reward as the handling fee for this operation."],["Mercenary Broker","Of course, once you deliver the money, you'll enjoy exclusive rights to this bounty, so no other mercenary will compete with you."],["Ann","Exclusive... Now that sounds good."],["Ann","But I already spent all the money I could borrow to buy this ST... I'm afraid I don't have the funds for this fee."],["","Upon hearing this, the agent quickly opened Ann's Skynet information and swiftly scanned through the account section."],["Mercenary Broker","(Muttering) Tsk, really... Looks like someone beat me to it and picked 'em clean... guess I've no choice then..."],["Mercenary Broker","Don't worry, you still have an ST in your hands, right? That's a valuable asset too."],["Mercenary Broker","How about this? I'll take a loss, and you can mortgage the ownership of this ST to us as the handling fee for this time."],["Ann","But if you can't pay it back, then this ST will..."],["Mercenary Broker","Haha, losing faith already? Look on the bright side, as long as you complete this bounty, you'll get the deposit back with interest."],["Mercenary Broker","Or... do you want to miss this opportunity that's handed to you?"],["Ann","True, the enemies are just third-rate mercenaries, nothing to worry about!"],["Mercenary Broker","Alright, I have confirmed your collateral receipt. Now let me send over the relevant intel about GKD Parcel Service."],["Ann","Wow, how amazing... so many things suddenly appeared on my screen!"],["Ann","Well, no time to waste. I'm heading off right away! Bye—!"],["","Watching Ann's departing figure, the agent finally dropped the business-like expression and revealed a sly smile."],["Mercenary Broker","Hahaha, what a joke, even waved goodbye to me..."],["Mercenary Broker","Sigh, don't blame me, blame yourself for stepping onto this island without knowing anything."],["Mercenary Broker","In Milkhama, fools like you exist only to feed others... So let GKD Parcel Service send you on your way."]],"560325401":[["","DL Military Base"],["","Interrogation Number: DL-K-092   Subject: Ann Olam  Identity: Illegal Immigrant"],["Victoria","I'll ask you again—what is the purpose of GKD Parcel Service seizing \"Nephthys\"?"],["Ann","Ah..."],["Victoria","Who's tipping you off? Who's leaking classified DL intel to you? Answer me—how did you learn the location of this classified ST?!"],["Victoria","Was it those Vesper terrorists? No, even that traitor Tiphys didn't have this sort of clearance. Could it be... her?!"],["Ann","Well, this..."],["Victoria","I need to know all about your contacts, hideouts, and armories along the way!"],["Ann","I-I..."],["Victoria","Speak! If you want to live, tell me everything in detail!"],["Ann","My only connection with GKD Parcel Service was picking up their bounty at the Mercenary Broker, and then I ran into the target named Grant on the way..."],["Ann","Then halfway through the fight, you guys caught me... Other than that, I really know nothing about them!"],["Ann","I also bought this ST at the market, and I raised a lot of money to get it... Can you give it back to me?"],["Victoria","Oh, another pathetic lie. It seems you don't realize the situation you're in."],["","Victoria clenched her teeth."],["","Clearly, the answer didn't satisfy her."],["Victoria","The \"Nephthys\" you're piloting is a prototype equipped with the DL's secret technology..."],["Victoria","To get it, GKD Parcel Service was willing to raid our lab, stepping into the lion's den, knowing full well they risked being cut off and besieged within."],["Victoria","You're telling me now that after they went through all that trouble for this ST, they threw it in the depot and forgot about it? And you just happened to pop in and buy it?!"],["","Ann's brain was racing, trying to recall every detail of purchasing the ST."],["","But despite racking her brain, she still couldn't remember anything suspicious."],["Ann","Yes, it's true... That's all I know!"],["Ann","I'm not a partner of GKD Parcel Service at all, you've got the wrong person!"],["Victoria","Nonsense!"],["Ann","I... I'm really not lying... *sob*"],["","Having spent her whole life outside the island, this was all new to Ann."],["","Under Victoria's aggressive questioning, she burst into tears."],["Ann","I just arrived on the island today... I really don't know anything..."],["Ann","Finally got an ST, finally got the bounty... I just wanted to work and make some money...*sob*"],["Victoria","......"],["","Looking at the girl sobbing in fear before her, Victoria showed not a hint of sympathy; instead, her expression grew increasingly grim."],["Victoria","Stop your pathetic whimpering!"],["Victoria","Work? Money? Do you think Milkhama is some amusement park where you can come and go as you please?!"],["Victoria","I arrived on this island at your age, and since the first day I set foot here, I haven't retreated from the front lines."],["Victoria","When my ST's engine was damaged by the NDF and they pointed their guns at the cockpit... I didn't shed a single tear or beg for mercy."],["","At this point, Victoria's gaze turned cold as she looked at the adjutant beside her."],["Victoria","Since she doesn't want to talk, let's not waste time on this."],["Victoria","Implant the <yellow>experimental chip</yellow> in her and throw her into the experimental zone to fend for herself."],["DLAF Deputy","Lieutenant, is this... really okay?"],["DLAF Deputy","I just retrieved the data from the civilian database, and a lot of it corroborates her account. Based on the information we have, she is indeed a stowaway who arrived on the island only today."],["Victoria","That's hard to say. No one knows if this is a story she specifically created to cover her identity... The DL can't afford to make any mistakes right now."],["Victoria","Besides, as I understand it, there has never been an innocent stowaway. If she were truly as gentle as she claims, she wouldn't have set foot on this island in the first place."],["Victoria","Stowaways, like those rebellious Milkhamans, are breeding grounds for corruption and instability. The DL has no room for them."],["Victoria","Let them serve their limited purpose in the underground laboratory."],["DLAF Deputy","Understood, I will prepare immediately."],["Victoria","Additionally, remind the reconnaissance squad to keep an eye on the movements of the GKD Parcel Service."],["Victoria","I've crossed swords with them before, in the Central Mining Area. Though mere mercs, their skill rivals the West Island regulars... they won't give up easily."],["","At the same time, Kelvin City border depot."],["","Since breaking away from the DLAF's encirclement, Grant has encountered almost no effective resistance besides a few scattered pursuers."],["","After repeatedly confirming there were none on his tail, Grant finally returned to the border warehouse used as a safe house."],["","He had originally planned to get home, put his feet up, and crack open a few cold ones... but as soon as he opened the hatch, he was met with the sound of a heated argument."],["Kaidan","Harvey! You sold that \"Nephthys\" we fought so hard for just 2 million Milkhama dollars?!"],["Harvey","Well... 1.8 million. I saw she was hesitating, so I gave her a discount."],["Kaidan","That's just great! Should I thank you on behalf of that stowaway, Captain Generous?!"],["Harvey","Stop it, stop it! I know I was wrong... I just wanted to earn some operational funds for everyone... I didn't expect it to turn out like this!"],["Grant","Woah! What's going on here? What's all this arguing?"],["Grant","I was gonna have a drink to celebrate, but the atmosphere here is rowdier than a bar-room brawl!"],["Dana","Grant... We're in big trouble."],["Grant","Don't worry. No matter how big the issue is, all we need to do is sit down and calmly think it through."],["Grant","Both of you, calm down, okay? Tell me what happened."],["","The story of the journey was quickly told, but... the atmosphere became even more tense."],["","Even the usually carefree Grant now had a hint of unease on his face."],["Grant","So, that's how it is, huh..."],["Grant","You followed the plan and brought \"Nephthys\" to the depot, but an emergency occurred and you didn't have time to inform Harvey... so you just parked it somewhere."],["Grant","As for Harvey, she just happened to step in afterwards... and the customer coincidentally took a liking to that particular ST. So, without knowing, Harvey sold her the ST. Something like that?"],["Harvey","That's it."],["Harvey","I apologize! But... in summary, I'm not the only one responsible for this..."],["Grant","At this point, let's not pass the buck. We're all in the same boat, and no one wants to see this situation."],["Grant","Let's first think about how to retrieve this ST."],["Dana","Harvey, do you have the buyer's identity information? Since she borrowed money, Skynet should have a record."],["Dana","Whether we go soft or hard next... as long as we can contact her directly, things will be much easier to handle."],["Harvey","There is indeed a record, but... the person just arrived on the island today."],["Harvey","Even if we dig through Skynet, all we can find is information from this afternoon."],["Dana","Then try to recall if there are any other useful clues, even the tiniest details."],["Harvey","Let me think about that first..."],["","From sabotaging the cargo hold to persuading her to buy an ST... Harvey carefully recalls every word exchanged with her."],["","Every action has a motive, and the motive of this stowaway is—"],["Harvey","Oh! I remember! She mentioned that the reason she came to the island, the reason she bought that ST... was for gold! To get rich!"],["Harvey","That's why I specifically pitched the ST to her and even introduced her to the mercenary business."],["Harvey","However, with her skills, she probably can't do anything decent. Nine times out of ten, she'll be fooled and end up doing some shady bounty jobs."],["Grant","Newcomer, mercenary, bounty... These words sound familiar..."],["","Listening to Harvey's description, Grant couldn't help but recall that reckless pilot who charged right towards the guns of the DLAF."],["Grant","That \"Nephthys\"... Do you have any photos or similar information? I'd like to take a look."],["Harvey","Of course, I will synchronize it to you right away."],["","Arms equipped with wings, a composite structure... Grants suspicions were confirmed—it wasn't the first time he'd seen this ST."],["","He finally realized why the DLAF were so intimidated after seeing that ST."],["Grant","Well, I've got good news and bad news."],["Grant","The good news is, I've encountered this ST before, and as Harvey said, the pilot is a girl who just arrived on the island."],["Kaidan","Grant, cut the suspense... You've seen this \"Nephthys,\" now where is it?!"],["Grant","Sigh, that's the bad news..."],["Grant","That girl must've been duped by someone. She was harpin' on about catching me, claiming my bounty—the whole shebang. Then, wouldn't you know it—she ran straight into their hands."],["Grant","That ST... the DLAF have got it back."],["Kaidan","What?!"]],"560326101":[["","Silly kid. Gold mining is just like any job. Of course there are hiccups along the way."],["","Collapse, flooding, arguments, deceit... Whenever we relax, this island always arranges some natural or man-made disasters to teach us a lesson."],["","Ann, remember, when you encounter problems you can't solve... don't hesitate to ask for help and seek assistance from others."],["","No gold miner succeeds with just a shovel in hand."],["","DL Military Base Detention Area"],["","Am... am I still alive?"],["","Pain, sorrow. The girl quietly crouches in the corner, the recent encounter still wandering her mind."],["","Victoria's interrogation didn't last long. After she lost her patience, a group of people in white coats took over the follow-up work."],["","They treated Ann like an experiment animal, strapping her tightly to the operating table and implanting something into her body."],["","After that, Ann couldn't remember much... She only recalled those people constantly muttering about \"materials,\" \"data,\" and \"brain screening.\""],["","When she fully regained consciousness, she found herself in an unfamiliar room filled with the strong smell of disinfectant."],["Ann","Why did things turn out this way...?"],["Ann","I came here to become a gold miner like Grandpa and make a name for myself, but now...?"],["Ann","I've lost my money, my ST has been confiscated, and I'm being treated like a guinea pig, thrown into this surgery-like place..."],["Ann","If this keeps up, will I die...?"],["Ann","I kind of... want to go home..."],["","Bang!"],["","Just as Ann was sinking into depression, a series of strange tremors suddenly echoed through the room, as silent as a grave."],["Ann","Huh? What's that sound? Over by the vent... something's there?"],["","Ann, who had been sitting idle, was drawn to the sudden noise and curiously leaned against the wall. The muffled sound gradually became clearer."],["","It was a continuous, chaotic scraping sound... like two apprentice carpenters sawing wood for the first time, not knowing where to apply force, just huffing and puffing back and forth."],["","Are you sure this is the right place? My drill just got jammed!"],["","You picked the wrong gear! Turn off auto mode and switch to manual!"],["","Oh, oh! It's moving! See, it takes more than something like this to stop me... Come on—break!"],["","Fool! Don't drill there! That's the load-bearing part of the vent! It's gonna collapse—"],["","The sound of friction suddenly intensified, then quickly turned into the heavy thud of a foreign object hitting the ground."],["","Two flamboyantly styled men crashed down to the floor one after the other, along with their crude escape tools."],["Fenrir","...Movme! What the hell are you doing...?! I must've been crazy to break out with you!"],["Movme","*cough* How is this my fault?! You're the one who wanted to drill through that spot—if I was alone I'd be long gone!"],["Fenrir","Just mindlessly drilling like it's no big deal. Are you that dense? Haven't the guards beaten you enough yet?"],["Ann","Um... excuse me..."],["Movme","Where did this little girl come from? Hey—don't interrupt us while we're arguing!"],["Fenrir","You blockhead, we've ended up in someone else's room! Wait—she isn't going to call the guards, is she?!"],["","As the words came out, Fenrir and Movme suddenly felt nervous. They quickly grabbed their escape tools."],["","In contrast, the owner of the cell showed no sign of caution, approaching them eagerly as if seeing a savior."],["Ann","Are you breaking out? Could you... take me with you?"],["Fenrir","Huh?!"],["","Whether it was Ann's harmless demeanor or the exhaustion from their earlier struggle, the two found themselves unable to refuse her."],["","The two simply sat on the ground, repairing the electric drill in hand while engaging in a casual conversation with their fellow inmate."],["Ann","So... you plan to crawl all the way out through the ventilation ducts?"],["Fenrir","That was the plan, yes. But because of that fool Movme, we lost our only ladder. The plan won't work without it."],["Movme","Why are you blaming me again? You said it yourself: wherever you point, I drill. If you're gonna blame someone, blame yourself!"],["Ann","Also, I have one more question... Where exactly is this place?"],["Ann","Supposed to be a hospital but also some kinda prison. I asked those guards a few times, but they wouldn't tell me anything."],["Fenrir","Ha, you seriously don't know?"],["Fenrir","This... is the DL's <yellow>\"Landfill\"</yellow>."],["Fenrir","Defiant natives, mercenaries with sensitive identities, unfortunate souls who saw things they shouldn't... Oh, and those terrorists who call themselves Vesper."],["Fenrir","Anyone they can't deal with legally but want to get rid of—they throw them in here to fend for themselves."],["Fenrir","But..."],["","At this point, Fenrir took a moment to size up Ann... She wasn't like any of the other prisoners; it was like she didn't really belong here."],["Fenrir","However, you don't seem to have any ties with the DL, do you?"],["Fenrir","What did you do to end up here?"],["Ann","I..."],["","After settling down, she told them about how she pursued the GKD Parcel Service only to be arrested by the Defense Force."],["Fenrir","GKD?! If you want bragging rights, pick a different target. They're... not someone a little girl like you should be messing with."],["Movme","Don't make me laugh. Even I have to think twice before taking them on! You fought them? They could beat you blindfolded!"],["Ann","I... I'm not lying, I have proof!"],["","Ann reached down, taking a neatly-folded note from her pocket. At the first opportunity, Fenrir snatched it from her hands and opened it."],["Fenrir","A bounty notice? What century is this? People still use these...?"],["Movme","Hahaha, I told you. As if this girl would have the guts to pick a fight with people like that. Right, Fenrir?"],["Movme","Fenrir? What's wrong with you, speak up!"],["Fenrir","This thing... It's real. It even has Harpy's seal on it. You can't get this certificate without spending money."],["Ann","...So what about you guys, why were you locked up?"],["Movme","......"],["Fenrir","......"],["","Now it was the Electric Eel guys' turn to be put on the spot."],["","Seeing Movme about to open his mouth, Fenrir shot him a look."],["Movme","(whispering) ...What's wrong?"],["Fenrir","(whispering) You... You're not really gonna tell her, are you? It's too embarrassing!"],["Movme","(whispering) So what are you going to do? You can't just leave her hanging, right?"],["Fenrir","(whispering) Let me make something up... Work with me, okay?"],["","Fenrir patted Movme on the shoulder and coughed a few times theatrically."],["Fenrir","Want to know how we ended up locked in here? Well, that's a long story..."],["Fenrir","It was an event that took place in the west of Milkhama Island, within the jurisdiction of the UNCS."],["Frida","Alright, little eels, I've settled the price with our client—time to get to work!"],["Frida","Movme, the mobile unit on the left is yours to handle... Remember, keep a low profile. Wait until the enemy enters the ambush zone before opening fire."],["Frida","If you make such a rookie mistake again, my bat's making contact with your skull."],["Frida","As for Fenrir, you're in charge of guarding our flank. Don't argue—what I want is..."],["Fenrir","Hold on a second! What kind of story are you spinning? You're making us look bad!"],["Movme","But... doesn't the boss usually order us around like this?"],["Fenrir","Boss? Frida is no longer our boss!"],["Fenrir","When you're out there, your identity is what you make it... Come on, broaden your horizons a bit!"],["Jungle Overlord Fenrir","Ms. Frida, since when do you get to command me?"],["Jungle Overlord Fenrir","Have you already forgotten? The Electric Eel mercenary group only exists today because of my past leniency. You're lucky I didn't wipe you out."],["Jungle Overlord Fenrir","And after all that, you're still being disrespectful?"],["Frida?","...Of course I haven't forgotten."],["Frida?","It was you who brought order to the Northwest Jungle, supporting the Electric Eel mercenary group on the brink of collapse... All mercenaries regard you as a legend."],["Jungle Overlord Fenrir","Well... from now on, I'm in charge. Do you have any objections?"],["Frida?","Of course not. As the world's greatest mercenary, strategist, tactician, military expert, commander and pilot... Electric Eel should follow your lead to the letter."],["Movme","Woah, man. That's one long list of people."],["Jungle Overlord Fenrir","Those are titles—titles! If you don't understand, don't interrupt!"],["Blair?","Major, if I remember correctly, I said all mercenaries disturbing order in the UNCS must be eradicated. All of them."],["Blair?","So why are our lines still infested with mercenaries?"],["William?","I fully admit it... As frontline commander, this stalemate is something I cannot shirk responsibility for."],["William?","In our original plan, it was presumed they wouldn't last more than 10 minutes under our bombardment."],["William?","Yet on the western battlefield, there's a damn ST that seems to have wings. No matter how we tighten our firepower net, it always manages to escape!"],["William?","Give me another chance, and I'll crush this maggot!"],["Mercenary King Movme","Why don't you go ahead and give it a try!"],["William?","Damn, when did he break through the defenses, ugh—"],["Fenrir","Wait, isn't your story a bit too exaggerated?!"],["Fenrir","He's a dignified NDF major, and you treat him like a sitting duck?"],["Movme","You said it yourself, when you're out there, your identity is what you make it!"],["Movme","I'll make up whatever I want. Anyway, I've been fed up with these NDF guys for a long time!"],["Blair?","Impossible! The army I've led through countless battles, my carefully deployed plan... all ruined by a mercenary..."],["Mercenary King Movme","Have you witnessed the might of the Mercenary King?!"],["Mercenary King Movme","I don't care if you're a major or a governor—mess with Movme the Great and you're dead!"],["Fenrir","Anyway, that's me and Movme's story."],["Fenrir","You probably understand now, right?"],["Ann","But... if you're so powerful, why are you locked up here?"],["","As if hit in a sore spot, Fenrir, who had been speaking eloquently, hesitated and stammered."],["Fenrir","It's because... w-well, you see... we've been framed!"],["Fenrir","Do you remember that Frida from Electric Eel? She's the one who got us in this mess!"],["Fenrir","Originally, we had no opponents in West Milkhama, and to spread the fame of Electric Eel, Movme and I specifically came to the east."],["Fenrir","Without our knowledge, she secretly colluded with the Defense Forces and set up an ambush when we crossed the border... That's how we ended up in trouble."],["Movme","That's right! If it were a fair fight, even combined, they wouldn't be a match for us!"],["Ann","......"],["","After listening to Fenrir's explanation, Ann remained silent, lowering her head thoughtfully."],["Movme","(Whispering) Does she not believe it?"],["Fenrir","(Whispering) It's because you exaggerated too much! Look at what you said, kicking officers, punching governors... A three-year-old could make up a more believable story!"],["Movme","(Whispering) Oh, you're one to talk! Going on about how you're Jungle Overlord, like you're some bigwig. Lord of the jail cell more like! What a load of nonsense."],["Fenrir","(Whispering) That was artistic liberty! Don't you understand anything?"],["Movme","(Whispering) Stop arguing! She's looking over!"],["","Perhaps feeling guilty, Movme and Fenrir both turned their heads simultaneously, avoiding eye contact with her."],["Ann","You two..."],["Ann","You two really are legendary mercenaries! Even the stories my grandfather used to tell don't compare to the magic of your adventures!"],["","Ann's voice rose by almost twenty decibels, a cheer mixed with euphoria and surprise."],["Movme","Huh?!"],["Fenrir","This little girl... really believed it?!"],["","Seeing Ann like this, the two Electric Eels finally relaxed completely and continued to boast."],["Ann","So... not only the UNCS and the DL, but even that huge group called Obsidian has to look up to you?"],["Fenrir","Ahem, and that's just the tip of the iceberg... To tell our story, we'd need three days and three nights. And even then we'd still probably not be finished."],["Movme","Listen—maybe it's fate that we met here, why don't you join us?"],["Movme","I've already thought of a name for our group. Let's call it the <yellow>\"Super Electric Eels\"</yellow>! It's like the Electric Eels on steroids!"],["Ann","So if I join now, does that make me the third-in-command of Super Electric Eels?"],["Fenrir","That's right, once we make a fortune and become famous, you'll get your share of the profit!"],["","Saying this, Fenrir seemed to realize something, shifting his eyes toward the door."],["Fenrir","Actually, why hasn't the guard come yet? Usually when we make a racket, those guys come running and give us a beating."],["Fenrir","Weird. By now there should've been some action, yet nothing."],["Ann","Maybe something's happened? Did you hear those sounds outside? Like gunfire, explosives..."],["","As though prompted by Ann, Fenrir cautiously poked his head outside the iron door."],["","Unexpectedly, there was neither reprimand nor warning... not even a shadow of a guard outside."],["Fenrir","A golden opportunity..."],["","Fenrir gave Movme a look. He understood, swinging the wall-drilling tool at the lock of the iron door with force."],["","In no time, the door locking the room was riddled with holes, and after a few more kicks from Fenrir and Movme, it completely lost its function as a door."],["Movme","Hmph, there's no door in this world that can keep me locked in!"],["Fenrir","By the way, Ann, the reason the Defense Force is after you, it's because they have their eyes on the ST you bought?"],["Ann","Yeah, during the interrogation they kept yelling about top secret intel, a prototype ST, things like that... they were so aggressive I almost burst into tears."],["Fenrir","That settles it then. When we escape, that ST is our ride. I doubt it's stored that far away."],["Movme","Exactly! Take your ST with you! Those Defense Force bastards... I've been bottling this anger up for a long time—and I'm gonna vent it all on them!"],["Fenrir","That idiot..."],["","Fenrir furrowed his brow and quickly pulled his companion away from Ann, dragging him to the corner."],["Movme","What now?!"],["Fenrir","You... You didn't really take that Super Electric Eels talk seriously, did you?"],["Movme","What? Of course I did."],["Movme","Oh, I get it... You don't like the name I chose?"],["Fenrir","What's going on in that brain of yours? We came to the east to prove ourselves to those who looked down on us, not to recruit followers!"],["Movme","Oh, now that you mention it, that's true..."],["Fenrir","That girl said the reason she was captured was that DL military hardware... that thing is our leverage."],["Fenrir","Think about it, if we get our hands on that secret ST the Defense Force is developing... Will those guys still look down on us?"],["Fenrir","Once that girl finds the ST and drives it out of the barracks, we'll snatch it under the guise of protection fees... Simple as that."],["Movme","You crafty devil... So that was your plan!"],["Movme","Ruthless, insidious... Good idea, I'm in!"],["Fenrir","...Stay sharp on the way, don't let anyone get suspicious."],["","Meanwhile, DL Military Base..."],["Dana","Kaidan, I see the DL barracks. I've marked those patrolling STs and fixed checkpoints on the radar. Remember to stay in sync."],["Kaidan","Okay. Grant and I have just taken our positions. We'll receive your radar signal shortly."],["Kaidan","What about Harvey?"],["Harvey","It'll take a while. The coastline is crawling with Defense Force scouts... I need to find a safe spot to dock!"],["Harvey","But don't worry, it won't take too long. You can start the operation first."],["Kaidan","Alright. Dana, let's go over the operation plan once more."],["Kaidan","This mission is to reclaim \"Nephthys\" held at the military base."],["Kaidan","Next, Grant and I will deliberately expose our whereabouts and attack their patrols to draw the attention of the Defense Forces."],["Dana","I'll be on the frontlines. After you attract the main forces, I will penetrate the military base to regain control of the target ST."],["Kaidan","Remember, the clock will be ticking. We must complete the transfer before the Defense Forces realize what's happening."],["Dana","Wait, I hear the ST engines starting... They've noticed you!"],["Kaidan","These Defense Forces sure are quick off the mark."],["Kaidan","Then Grant and I will get to work... Dana, take care of your end!"]],"560326301":[["","Just dealing with Dana alone, the three of them had already given it their all. After losing their numerical upper hand, the hastily assembled team was soundly beaten by Kaidan and Grant."],["","The three founding members of the Super Electric Eels were thus escorted along with the ST to the container at the back of the truck."],["","According to GKD Parcel Service's plan, they will first be taken to the coast and then transferred to Harvey's ship."],["","However... This path ahead was not as calm as they expected."],["Ann","Give me back the ST... I paid for it, you can't just take it away!"],["Ann","I'm still in debt! Without my ST, my life is over! Give it back... give me back my ST... *sob*"],["Grant","That girl has been making a racket all afternoon... Boss, are we really just going to leave it like this?"],["Kaidan","How do you plan to handle it?"],["Kaidan","Run to the back and tell her something like..."],["Kaidan","Excuse me, that ST wasn't really for sale. The tech inside it is very important, so we're taking it back, no refunds. No hard feelings."],["Grant","I don't think that'll help the situation..."],["Kaidan","Well, think of it this way: what do we really know about this girl? Harvey said she's a total newbie but we have no way to verify that."],["Kaidan","Happening to pick that \"Nephthys,\" happening to run straight into the DL forces... A coincidence? Who knows?"],["Dana","Well look, if you really can't calm her down, just stuff her mouth with a rag. Letting this drag on won't solve anything."],["Kaidan","No need to be so rough. She'll probably tire herself out after a while."],["Kaidan","Besides, the STs were sold by Harvey, and she collected the money."],["Kaidan","Why should we do her dirty work? Let her clean up her own mess."],["Ann","They... don't seem to be responding?"],["Ann","Boss Fenrir, Boss Movme, is playing for sympathy really gonna work?"],["Fenrir","Just keep yelling. They're thin-skinned, they'll definitely come over soon."],["Ann","Alright, here I go!"],["","And so, the emotional cries echoed once more inside the cramped truck."],["","However, Movme was visibly displeased with the ruse thought up by his companions."],["Movme","What are you doing? Why are you making this little girl shout back and forth? I'm trying to sleep here!"],["Fenrir","That's exactly the effect we want... If you find it annoying, the GKD Parcel Service people will find it annoying too!"],["Fenrir","Make it even louder, and they'll lose it and kick us out... After all, we're not really the ones they're after."],["Movme","What, you're not taking that military cargo? I don't want to return to the west empty-handed!"],["Fenrir","You seriously plan to throw in with that kid? If you wanna profit from trouble, there's no shortage of opportunities on this island—let this one go!"],["Fenrir","Come on, pick up the pace. You, join in too—let's shout together!"],["","Fenrir took a deep breath and started banging against the bars that confined him, clanging incessantly."],["Fenrir","GKD Parcel Service, it's been so long. I didn't expect you would've sunken so far as to steal from a newcomer."],["Movme","Robbers! Bandits! Even I, Movme, don't stoop to stealing from little girls!"],["Movme","At least... not so far this month!"],["Kaidan","......"],["Kaidan","On second thought, never mind."],["Kaidan","Dana, go ahead and shut them up."],["Dana","...I was just thinking the same thing."],["Movme","Oh, here they come."],["Fenrir","See, I told you, if we keep howling, they'll start getting annoyed."],["Movme","But it looks like they're holding ropes and tape?"],["Dana","As you said... GKD Parcel Service isn't exactly a bunch of saints. We've done some rather shady things..."],["Dana","It's true. But the last people I want to hear that from is you, Movme and Fenrir!"],["Fenrir","You... No, not so rough... Ugh! Ugh!!!"],["Movme","No, no, sorry, we were just messing, no... Ugh!!!"],["","With their mouths and joints secured, the two of them were as well-wrapped as museum mummy exhibits."],["","Aside from the sound of breathing, they probably can't make any other noise."],["Dana","What about you? Do I need to come do you too?"],["Ann","No, no, that's alright!"],["Ann","I... I'll behave, honestly... From this point on, I'll stay quiet the whole time!"],["","By the time Victoria confirmed the anomaly and returned to the military base, the raid was already over."],["","The outer fortifications of the Defense Force base lay in ruins. The scent of explosives and charred debris hung in the air, and fragments of the brutal clash littered the ground."],["Victoria","Adjutant, talk to me."],["DLAF Deputy","The security soldiers left behind suffered heavy casualties, both companies were completely paralyzed... The patrol teams outside..."],["Victoria","Get to the point, I'm not here to assess asset losses!"],["DLAF Deputy","Yes, sir! The military camp was attacked by the GKD. The security forces present were taken out of commission. \"Nephthys\" is also confirmed missing."],["Victoria","Then why did it take twenty minutes after the incident for our troops to take action?!"],["DLAF Deputy","Well... their first step was to destroy our communications equipment, preventing the security forces present from contacting us."],["DLAF Deputy","Later, there was turmoil in the experiment area where prisoners were held, causing the outer troops to misjudge the situation and focus on the pursuit..."],["Victoria","Useless...!"],["","Victoria's boots stomped heavily on the charred remains, clenching her teeth tightly."],["DLAF Deputy","In addition, upon confirming that the attackers were GKD Parcel Service, I immediately ordered the nearby patrols to initiate a search."],["DLAF Deputy","But so far, we have found nothing."],["DLAF Deputy","These people have strong counter-reconnaissance capabilities. I'm afraid only a thorough search can determine their movements."],["DLAF Deputy","Should I begin the deployment immediately?"],["Victoria","No."],["","The adjutant assumed his no-nonsense officer would agree at once, but Victoria merely took a device from her waist and gazed at the screen, lost in thought."],["Victoria","Adjutant, you just mentioned there was an escape in the detention area."],["Victoria","Is the prisoner named \"Ann\" also on the list of escapees?"],["DLAF Deputy","Her? The area she was being held was indeed heavily damaged."],["DLAF Deputy","It's as the officer said. The prisoner took advantage of the chaos to escape."],["DLAF Deputy","But rest assured, our patrols have already recaptured 90% of the prisoners. In time, they will surely bring the remaining escapees to justice."],["Victoria","No need. Let them go."],["","Releasing tension, Victoria's eyebrows softened."],["Victoria","Prioritize treating the wounded and repairing damaged equipment. Gather the patrol teams from the perimeter—assemble all forces in this area."],["Victoria","And suspend the head of base security. From here on, this base is under my direct supervision."],["DLAF Deputy","But... Lieutenant, isn't our top priority to recover the \"Nephthys\"?"],["DLAF Deputy","But a plan like this is tantamount to letting the GKD Parcel Service escape!"],["","Faced with the adjutant's questioning, the usually stern Victoria barely reacted, responding only with a cold snort."],["Victoria","Then tell me, after these encounters, aside from the time they walked into our trap, have you achieved any results against GKD Parcel Service?"],["DLAF Deputy","......"],["Victoria","Adjutant, I don't doubt your loyalty to the DL, but incompetence is incompetence."],["Victoria","Shut up and do as I say."],["Victoria","I can assure you, GKD Parcel Service will definitely not escape our grasp!"],["Victoria","That prisoner... will lead us to them."]],"560327101":[["","Ann, don't take gold mining so lightly."],["","The descent down a mine is not pleasant at all, whether sitting in the rail car or inside the excavator... it's the same feeling."],["","You'll feel a surge of excitement at first, your mind running wild as you imagine what lies beneath the rock—could it be gold, jewels, or that arashium ore all the big shots are after?"],["","And the further you go, the deeper you sink, the darker your surroundings become, the more you start to feel the fear creeping in."],["","Afraid of the creaking equipment, afraid of the sounds in the darkness, afraid of sleeping forever underground... unable to return alive."],["","......"],["","Unfortunately, even Grandpa had no way around it. All we could do... was grit our teeth and endure."],["","Kaidan and his group traveled along the coastline and stopped at an abandoned port. Their captain companion had been waiting there for a long time."],["","After handing over the cargo and giving a brief explanation, Kaidan and his group piloted the STs back into the jungle outside the port."],["","The once vast abandoned port now only has Harvey—and the three people tied up tightly."],["Harvey","So, have you figured it out now?"],["Harvey","It's not that we don't want to sell it, but this ST was originally a secretly-developed ST that Kaidan and his team snatched from an underground laboratory!"],["Harvey","It's just that, due to... some unexpected circumstances, it ended up in your hands."],["Ann","So, from the beginning, you weren't telling me the truth, were you, Captain Harvey?"],["Harvey","......"],["Ann","Looking at it this way... all the debts I borrowed and the money I spent were for nothing. In the end, I still can't get this ST..."],["Harvey","Well, basically, yes... but we can handle it flexibly."],["Harvey","After all, the 1.8 million has already been credited, and it's quite troublesome to refund it... How about this, once things settle down, you can pick any one from my hangar as compensation."],["Ann","Really?!"],["Harvey","I'm being honest this time! After hearing about all you've been through, I feel really guilty. Let me show you some sincerity."],["","She nodded, the deal was struck, and the matter was quietly put aside... Exactly as Harvey intended."],["","Bu just then, the Electric Eel duo spoke up."],["Fenrir","That... might not be a good idea."],["Fenrir","On the West Island, everyone knows about Harvey's warehouse. Her ST stockpile is like a machinist's bad dream—outdated units no one can sel and heaps of junk no one can repair."],["Fenrir","How much can that scrap sell for? You sold her something of value, now you're trying to replace it with one of those duds?"],["Movme","Yeah! You say you feel guilty? If you feel so bad, let us go already!"],["Movme","The ST's in your hands now, so why keep us tied up like this getting blasted by the sea wind? What kind of treatment is this?!"],["","Seeing the deal falling through, Harvey put away her earlier enthusiasm and waved her hand."],["Harvey","...You think I really want you guys here?"],["Harvey","We've kept you this far because the Defense Forces were hot on our tail. What if we left you behind and you leaked intel?"],["Movme","What do you mean? You think we'd collaborate with the DL?"],["Harvey","Sure, if by \"collaborate\" you mean giving up all the info you have under torture. Don't worry, once Kaidan finishes up over there we're kicking you to the curb."],["Harvey","As for you..."],["","Harvey paused for a moment, then looked at Ann."],["","This innocent-looking girl seemed completely out of place between two slick, shameless Electric Eels."],["Harvey","Ann, Ann, Ann...I didn't expect you to exactly hit the ground running, but this is ridiculous. Electric Eel?! How did you get tangled up with people like them?"],["Harvey","Their reputation on this island is dreadful. \"Notorious\" would be a gross understatement."],["Fenrir","Captain Harvey, that's harsh. It's all in the game. Are you that different?"],["Movme","That's right! Who do you think you are? A ragged sailor on a rundown ship—what have you done that's so great? How dare you look down on us?!"],["Harvey","Hmph. Say what you like. At least I didn't waste all those years only to end up being chased off my own turf like a pair of stray dogs."],["Ann","Captain Harvey, that's enough!"],["Ann","Boss Fenrir, Boss Movme... they were framed and that's why they left the west—they're not stray dogs!"],["Ann","As Jungle Overlord and Mercenary King of this island, if they want to go back, it's just a matter of saying the word."],["Fenrir","Wait a minute, no need to say that... These are..."],["Ann","No, I insist on speaking, no one should disrespect you—even Captain Harvey!"],["","Like an opening floodgate, Ann became more and more enthusiastic, recounting everything Fenrir and Movme had said from start to finish."],["","In front of outsiders like Ann, Movme and Fenrir's nonsense might pass as a story. But in front of someone like Harvey who knows the truth... it's like a bad joke."],["","Before Ann could finish speaking, Harvey could not help but smirk."],["Harvey","Haha... Jungle Overlord? Mercenary King? Hahaha—it sounds like you two have been real busy! It's only been a month."],["Movme","Fenrir, this is all your fault..."],["Fenrir","Don't look at me... you weren't shy about boasting either..."],["","The two protagonists could think of nothing more to say. They lowered their heads in silence."],["Ann","Boss Fenrir, Boss Movme, why aren't you saying anything? Could it be..."],["Harvey","It's okay. If they won't speak, I will."],["Harvey","Ann, listen carefully. Let me tell you everything these two big shots have done."],["","A month ago, in UNCS jurisdiction..."],["","Movme and Fenrir, back when they were still \"Electric Eels\"..."],["Frida","Alright, little eels, I've settled the price with our client—time to get to work!"],["Frida","Movme, the mobile unit on the left is yours to handle... Remember, keep a low profile. Wait until the enemy enters the ambush zone before opening fire."],["Frida","If you make such a rookie mistake again, my bat's making contact with your skull."],["Frida","As for Fenrir, you're in charge of guarding our flank. Don't argue—what I want is..."],["Fenrir","Yes, yes! What you wanted was \"loyalty,\" \"obedience\"... But in the end, what did we get?"],["Fenrir","We've spent the whole year running around doing all kinds of ridiculous crap for you. We've worked our asses off, barely made a dime, and ended up in a load of trouble!"],["","A flicker of surprise crosses Frida's face, but she quickly regains her usual authority. She picks up her club and walks slowly over to Fenrir."],["Frida","That's because our former sponsor, Blair, was taken down. After that we've been stuck working under the GSA. These kind of jobs are all they ever threw our way."],["Frida","Don't like it? Then tell me your bright ideas. I'm all ears."],["Fenrir","......"],["Frida","I understand you're anxious. Things aren't as good as they were, it's true. But we have food, we have a roof over our heads. That's something."],["Frida","If I've got bread, even the smallest piece, you'll eat too. That's a promise."],["Movme","Bread?! Electric Eels need meat!"],["Movme","Boss, I hate to complain... but I have to say it. I don't think we can do this anymore!"],["Movme","How long have we been scavenging scrap metal in this desert?! We even have to hide when we fight! Are we Electric Eels or rats?"],["Frida","You'll have to bear with it—these days are nothing like before. You've seen what the new governor is capable of."],["Frida","That old kind of business... going near it now means death."],["Frida","Thanks to that job in the Central Mining Area, our relationship with the GSA has finally improved... so don't cause any more trouble."],["Fenrir","In the end, wasn't it your wrong bet in the first place? As the leader, you made a mistake, and now you're letting us members bear it."],["Frida","Fenrir, what exactly are you trying to say?"],["","As they talked, Frida had already discerned the meaning behind Fenrir's words. She tightly gripped the bat and stared directly at Fenrir."],["Fenrir","Then I'll get straight to the point... Movme and I plan to go solo."],["Frida","......"],["Fenrir","When the old leader died and you took out those competitors, I was happy... Happy that Electric Eel finally had someone sensible to lead us to great things."],["Fenrir","That's right, you have the means and the strength, but you've gotta also be fearless! After getting involved with the UNCS, you clung to it tightly, and even when Blair's ship was about to sink, you refused to let go!"],["Fenrir","After finally getting a new employer, what happened? It turned out to be that old fox Rosemary! Now we're like a dog, being ordered around by her!"],["Frida","Heh, I've seen plenty of your petty tricks... Do you really think you're qualified to say that?"],["Frida","Back then, Blair recruited more than just our mercenary group. The Mastiffs, Battle Axe Company, Wolf Fang Brotherhood... So many capable fighters."],["Frida","It's a pity, after the GSA came to power, where did all those swaggering fools go? They're gone. Kaput. Among so many people, only we, the Electric Eels, survived."],["Frida","What do you think made this possible?"],["Fenrir","......"],["Frida","Remember, even the worst ship is better than swimming in the sea. Blair or Mary Rose, they're just the ships carrying us."],["Frida","No one can be a winner forever... But I can keep you alive."],["","As Frida finished speaking, the previously restless crowd suddenly quieted down... Those who survived the Blair Rebellion knew very well what Electric Eel had relied on to persist until today."],["","As such, it seemed this unexpected clash was about to come to an end."],["Fenrir","W-who said anything about today?! It were aiming for tomorrow!"],["Fenrir","I won't waste any more words on you. Movme... let's go!"],["","Before the atmosphere completely cooled down, Fenrir gritted his teeth and led Movme straight out of the Electric Eel's camp."],["Fenrir","Anyone looking to make a fortune, come along! I guarantee to find you a good job, or my name's not Fenrir!"],["Fenrir","Old Jack, what did you call us here for today? Do you have new work for us?"],["Middleman","You're here... What about those followers you brought from Electric Eel? Only Movme is left?"],["Movme","You mean those ungrateful kids? They were complaining about having no money and no future, wanting to go back."],["Movme","So I just kicked them all out! With them gone, there are fewer people to split the money with."],["Movme","And I'm a partner, not a follower!"],["Middleman","Oh, that makes things much easier."],["","The Middleman let out a sigh of relief, took a stack of cash from his pocket, and threw it in front of the two."],["Middleman","Our partnership is over. Last time was the final job. Take the money and get lost."],["Fenrir","Hey, old Jack, what's going on?"],["Fenrir","We've completed all the tasks you sent us exactly as required... why're you suddenly turning your back on us?!"],["Middleman","Exactly as required? You've got a nerve!"],["Middleman","Last time, I told you to keep an eye on the mine from the depot. I said if those thieves come sneaking up, fire a few shots to scare them off."],["Middleman","And what happened? Oh yeah—you started shooting at everyone! Treating the employer's armory like your backyard! You blew up half the depot's ammunition for crying out loud!"],["Movme","We were provoked! If we didn't teach them a lesson, how would they remember?!"],["Middleman","And what about last week's incident? I told you to set up roadblocks, establish checkpoints, and keep the target outside the city..."],["Middleman","But you guys, you did no preparation beforehand, and when the target arrived, you just grabbed your weapons and chased! In front of half the city, you got blown up on the street with both people and machines!"],["Movme","So? Did we manage to keep them out or not?!"],["Middleman","The employer wanted discretion—discretion! Not to make headlines like you did!"],["Middleman","Do you think you're still with Electric Eel, doing whatever you want because Frida has your back?"],["","The Middleman's words seemed to touch a nerve, and Movme and Fenrir's faces suddenly turned grim."],["Fenrir","Frida, Frida, Frida! Why do you always bring her up, huh?!"],["Fenrir","How many times have we said it? We have no ties with Electric Eel anymore!"],["Movme","We're tougher than them and bolder than them! If you want to blame someone... blame yourself for assigning such lousy jobs!"],["","The Middleman seemed to have anticipated their reaction and responded with a cold laugh."],["Middleman","Oh? Is that really what you think?"],["Middleman","Let me be blunt, the only reason you're still standing here talking to me is because I'm doing Frida a favor."],["Middleman","If she hadn't appealed to me personally, asking me to look out for people from Electric Eel, I would've sent your sorry asses packing a long time ago!"],["Fenrir","Are you saying... the previous commissions were given to us only because of Frida?"],["Middleman","What else? There are plenty of mercenaries with two legs, you're not special... Do you really think you have something to offer?"],["Middleman","Now that the other Electric Eel people are gone, there's no need to continue this favor game... Get out of here, you're not welcome!"],["","Once they'd split from their old boss and crossed the Middleman, even the less selective employers would hesitate when they heard the names Fenrir and Movme..."],["","After enduring countless mockery and disdainful looks, the two had no choice but to leave the UNCS territory under the pretext of <yellow>\"cutting ties with the past\"</yellow>."],["","But before they could cross the border, the Defense Forces found them first."],["Fenrir","As I said, officer, we're mercenaries from the West Island. We're just here to make a living..."],["Fenrir","How about you look the other way and let us through?"],["","Fenrir sneaked over, pulling out a few lonely bills from his pocket."],["","The guard didn't so much as look at Fenrir, replying with a hard strike to the railing, shutting down Fenrir's effort."],["DL Soldier","Just a petty smuggler, and you dare to be slick here! Stay in the corner and don't think about playing tricks!"],["Movme","I knew I shouldn't have trusted you back then! You said you had a way to the East Island... Turns out, it was just a hiking trip?!"],["Movme","Great, now we've being treated as illegal immigrants!"],["Fenrir","Who knew their border got so strict! In the past, crossing it was like taking a stroll in the park."],["Fenrir","Besides, what right do you have to blame me?! Wasn't it you who said, \"If this place won't have me, another will\"? Now we're actually doing it, you're chickening out?"],["Movme","Ha, nothing has ever scared me—not since I was a kid!"],["Fenrir","Then it's settled. Don't worry, the situation with the DL is crazy right now... They won't do anything to us. In fact, they'll probably let us go soon."],["","As Fenrir said, they didn't wait long before a person dressed as a sergeant came over, seemingly to announce something."],["DLAF Deputy","Soldier, have you confirmed the identities of these two border jumpers?"],["Fenrir","See, their officer is coming now."],["DL Soldier","Their identities have already been found in the database. Both have detailed records on file; they're mercenaries who landed with the UNCS."],["Fenrir","I told you, right? Let's keep watching, they might even hire us instead. You know, there aren't many mercenaries as skilled as us in the east..."],["DL Soldier","After examining their records, we found that their mercenary group is called Electric Eel. They once served the former governor in the west, Blair, and have a long history of joint ops with the NDF."],["DL Soldier","...After Blair's internal conflict ended, they quickly began collaborating with the GSA. They were also present in the chaos at the Central Mining Area."],["DLAF Deputy","So that makes them UNCS spies?"],["DLAF Deputy","Then we must deal with them severely, erase their records, and detain them in the experimental area. We can't allow them any chance to leak information."],["Movme","Fenrir, this isn't... exactly what you had in mind, is it?"],["Fenrir","...Spies? W-wait! This is a misunderstanding, a misunderstanding!"],["Fenrir","The situation in the Central Mining Area was Frida acting on her own. We've already distanced ourselves from her. You can't...! Stop! Please let me explain——!"],["","By the time Harvey finished telling the story, the port was already dead silent."],["","Once she'd finished sharing the bits of Electric Eel gossip she'd heard in passing, Harvey left looking quite pleased with herself."],["","Neither Fenrir nor Movme made another move; they simply slumped against their posts, defeated."],["Ann","So..."],["","Eventually Ann broke the awkward silence."],["Ann","So, is what Harvey said true...?"],["Ann","You couldn't make it on your own turf, so you had to cross the river and try your luck. You ended up running into the patrol on the other side and got caught as illegal immigrants..."],["Fenrir","......"],["Movme","......"],["","They exchanged glances."],["","Fenrir, who lies as easily as drinking water, no longer has his previous pretentious demeanor, hanging his head to avoid Ann's eyes."],["","Movme clenched his fists, silently lowering his head, no longer showing his previous arrogance."],["","Those glamorous stories never belonged to these two mercs. They're just a couple of Electric Eels struggling in the mud..."],["Fenrir","How should I put it... It's a complicated situation. It's not something that can be explained in a few words. Movme and I actually..."],["Movme","Fenrir, that's enough."],["Movme","How long are you going to keep deceiving this little girl?!"],["Fenrir","......"],["","Movme lifted his head, speaking each word with a slow, measured intent."],["","Even a rogue has self-respect. Fenrir could tell that his companion no longer wanted to play along with this charade."],["Ann","So, being Jungle Overlord and Mercenary King... is that also made-up?"],["Movme","Fake, all fake! It's all stuff Fenrir and I made up to save face!"],["Movme","Just like Harvey said, we're the worst, the lowest, the most pathetic rogues you'll ever come across!"],["Movme","Chasing after a bit of face, greedy for a bit of reward, shouting about going independent—but without the boss we were useless! So we ended up as a pair of two-bit mercenary thugs."],["Ann","......"],["","Ann silently lowered her head. Soon, the dock returned to its previous dead silence... only this time, the silence was tinged with a sense of self-abandonment."],["","Seeing the other party gradually become dispirited, Fenrir stopped talking and pulled Movme into a corner where no one would notice."],["Fenrir","Movme, that was too much... You've scared off our little follower."],["Movme","Whatever, anyway, I feel much better after telling the truth... If I'd known, I wouldn't have bragged with you back then."],["Movme","Forget it, let's not talk about this. Back to business... What should we do next?"],["Fenrir","What else can we do? Find a way to leave. Or do you enjoy being bound to a post?"],["Movme","What next? The DL side is out of reach... Are you planning to return empty-handed?"],["Fenrir","…Of course not. I have some tools left over from when we were digging in that duct; they're in my pocket... I'll use these to get outta here later."],["Fenrir","Since we're here, let's grab some stuff first... And keep it quiet, don't get that little girl involved. We'll move after she falls asleep. Dragging her along is pointless."],["Movme","Understood, leave it to me. We'll do it when Harvey is distracted!"],["","Of course, these Electric Eels struggling in the mud aren't discouraged easily. After a few words, they regained their usual fighting spirit."],["Ann","......"],["","So much so that they didn't realize a certain girl had noticed their plan..."]],"560327301":[["DLAF Deputy","Report, Lieutenant. We have fully secured the port that was privately occupied by GKD Parcel Service."],["DLAF Deputy","The ST \"Nephthys\" stolen by GKD Parcel Service was also found in the cargo hold they abandoned. It's currently undergoing intake."],["Victoria","Well done, adjutant."],["DLAF Deputy","Lieutenant, I'm curious about something."],["DLAF Deputy","How... did you find this place?"],["DLAF Deputy","An old port, abandoned for years... Even those seasoned patrolmen didn't notice this place."],["DLAF Deputy","If it weren't for you standing your ground at the operational meeting, we would have been played by GKD Parcel Service again."],["Victoria","I told you, didn't I: \"That prisoner will lead us to them.\""],["Victoria","I never go back on my promises."],["Victoria","Adjutant, do you remember the thing I had you implant in the prisoner?"],["DLAF Deputy","That chip?!"],["","Victoria snorted coldly and took out the tracker—a faint light was flickering not far away."],["Victoria","I said at the time that this stowaway has deep ties with GKD Parcel Service, and their connection is far from simple as she claims."],["Victoria","Thanks to this bait, we caught the big fish."],["Victoria","Alright, once the finishing touches are done, retract the troops and start the transfer immediately. The patrols sent out can be withdrawn."],["DLAF Deputy","But... GKD Parcel Service is still at large. Doesn't a passive strategy put us at a disadvantage?"],["Victoria","Passive? It's precisely because these soldiers are so incompetent that we have to adopt such tactics!"],["Victoria","In front of the GKD Parcel Service, their search is as useless as a game of hide and seek! Those good-for-nothings are only fit to plug holes in the frontline."],["Victoria","Keep a close watch, \"Nephthys\" has slipped from our grasp twice already... I won't tolerate any more mistakes."],["DLAF Deputy","Understood, this time... I won't let you down."],["","Meanwhile, on the other side, the Electric Eel group took advantage of the recent chaos and slipped away."],["","The three sat around on a nearby hill, watching the commotion at the port with great excitement."],["Movme","What a spectacle! It's the first time I've seen so many defense troops!"],["Fenrir","Only those guys from GKD Parcel Service could cause such a big mess."],["Fenrir","Let's stay here a while longer. We'll go down after the defense troops disperse. Otherwise, we might be mistaken for their comrades and get attacked."],["Ann","But... what about my ST? Am I just going to hand it over to the defense troops?"],["Fenrir","What else do you expect? You want to go head-to-head with the regular army? Do you have a death wish?"],["Ann","R-Right..."],["Fenrir","But then again... back at the dock, you actually came back to help us out."],["Fenrir","Didn't I tell you that all those stories were just fairy tales? Don't you think we'll just trick you again? Was once not enough?"],["Ann","Nah, not really. Though mainly I just don't have anywhere else to go, haha..."],["Ann","Besides, I think... you're not as bad as you say you are."],["Movme","Ha, getting tricked by someone then coming to their defense... Little girl, do you have a screw loose?"],["Ann","No! I was just... speaking from the heart."],["Ann","The time I've spent on Milkhama, it's been just about a day."],["Ann","In this day... I've been intimidated by mercenaries, deceived by Harvey, swindled by agents, and even captured by those regular troops as a test subject..."],["Ann","Among all the people I've met, only you sincerely paid attention to me, saying you want to establish a new Electric Eel and make a name on Milkhama Island together."],["Fenrir","Didn't I say? That was fake too... We're no more noble than those who messed with you."],["Fenrir","That was all just talk to trick you into joining and let your guard down. Our original plan was to rob that military cargo from you as soon as we left the camp."],["Fenrir","You probably understand by now, there's no good person on Milkhama Island. Those who could be called that are either dead in a grave or rotting in the mud."],["Fenrir","The only ones left are scumbags like us."],["Ann","But out of all those people, it was you two \"scumbags\" who helped me..."],["Ann","Not only did you help me escape from the lab, but you even went and wrestled with those guys from GKD Parcel Service."],["Fenrir","I told you, it's because we have our eyes on your ST! What aren't you getting, kid?"],["Ann","Because Grandpa said that a gold miner relies not only on the shovel in their hand, but also... the people who travel with them."],["Fenrir","Grandpa?"],["","Ann didn't rush to answer but instead looked towards the distant horizon."],["Ann","It's because of Grandpa and the stories he told... that I came to this island."],["Ann","Back then, this island didn't seem as... complicated as it is now."],["Ann","At that time, as long as you could gather a team and pay a fee, you could contract the mining rights for a piece of land."],["Movme","Gold? Mines? Was there ever such good fortune on this island?"],["Fenrir","Aren't you listening? That was from her grandfather's time... back when the border wars hadn't even started."],["Fenrir","Back then, gold mining was as simple as planting trees in your backyard. As long as you had the will, anyone could go to the island and get a share."],["Ann","It wasn't all easy, though. At that time, the island was like a wasteland, lacking people, money, and technology."],["Ann","Grandpa said that during the lowest point, the mine lacked even a single excavation ST."],["Fenrir","Then what did you rely on for gold mining? You couldn't have really dug by hand, could you?"],["Ann","What Grandpa and the others relied on was..."],["","Well, Ann, there were many reasons the Olam Mine managed to get up and running—it was the timing, the investors willing to take a gamble, those excavation STs that had only just become available..."],["","But most importantly, I think... it was the people."],["","Hahaha, don't get the wrong idea... Grandpa's friends weren't quite as extraordinary as you might imagine."],["","They called themselves gold miners... but at the end of the day, they were just a bunch of drifters from all over."],["","Someone who originally did business, got set up, ended up in debt, and chose to take their last bit of cash to the island for one final gamble."],["","A man who committed a crime was supposed to be hanged on the gallows, but he quickly outsmarted his captors and hid in the ship's cabin before the execution... Only after disembarking did he realize he had arrived in Milkhama."],["","Another one had parents who were both doctors, but he grew tired of the endless disinfectant and white coats, choosing to come here for excitement."],["","Some were responsible for raising funds, some for recruiting workers, some for drilling down the mines, and some for handling the excavators... Everyone found a way to do something."],["","It was precisely people like that, people with nowhere to go and no choices left, this group of madmen who saw gold mining as their last chance in life, that managed to get the Olam Mine up and running—albeit with some bumps along the way."],["","Here, no one asks where you're from. Whether you're looking to get rich overnight, you've been backed into a corner, or simply have nowhere else to go—as long as you're willing to pick up a shovel, you're part of the mine... part of the gold miners."],["Ann","......"],["Ann","Grandpa's Olam Mine was started... with this very spirit."],["Ann","It's the same now. I don't care if you're a legendary mercenary or a lowly rogue; those are just meaningless titles."],["Ann","All I know is that in the laboratory, at the military base, at the docks, you helped me and saved my life... For that alone, I have no reason to look down on you."],["Fenrir","......"],["Movme","......"],["","This time, it was the two Electric Eels who fell silent."],["","After a long while, Fenrir finally opened his mouth, as if relieved."],["Fenrir","Pretty ironic, huh? I've been lying my way through this island for most of my life, spinning tales for anyone and anything. But somehow now, for the first time, I've got no lie to tell."],["Fenrir","Scoundrels like us, respected...? Ha! Is it me or has the world gone mad?"],["Fenrir","You really have no idea how the world works, girl... Explaining it to you would be pointless."],["Movme","Oh, getting embarrassed?"],["Movme","I need to make something clear! We were definitely bragging about those other things before, but what I said about the Super Electric Eels is all true! If you're interested, you're welcome anytime."],["Fenrir","Are you crazy? The work we do is not something this little girl can handle. Do you want her to die faster?"],["Movme","Then... just have her serve tea and water. When I first joined Electric Eel, that's how I got by, right? Look at me now, I can stand on my own!"],["","But just as the two are looking forward to the future, the sound of an ST climbing onto the muddy ground suddenly comes from the side."],["","The sound was faint, deliberately hidden beneath the sea breeze... a feat only accomplished by the most experienced pilots."],["Fenrir","Cut the chatter, fool! The Defense Force... they're coming!"],["Movme","Damn it, didn't these guys get what they wanted? Don't they have anything better to do?!"],["","Without a word, the two grabbed the gunports on the STs, firing wildly at the shadows, until the rustling from the forest went quiet."],["Movme","Did we get them?"],["Fenrir","Wait! Stay sharp!"],["","The rustling returned, intensified; far from disappearing, the sound drew closer through the smoke... until the three of them finally saw their target."],["Kaidan","Unfortunately, this time, it was not the Defense Force."],["Fenrir","Kaidan?! What the hell are you doing here?!"],["Fenrir","The ST you're looking for isn't with us. If you're here to collect a debt, you've got the wrong people."],["Kaidan","No, I'm right on target."],["Kaidan","The one I'm looking for... is the young girl behind you."]],"560328101":[["Harvey","Wait, did I hear that right?"],["Harvey","Do you really suspect... Ann is a spy planted by the Defense Force?"],["Kaidan","I've thought about it for a long time. The ship was prepared on the spot, and we selected that port spontaneously, having only found it recently... The Defense Forces are not mind-readers. There's no way they could've tracked us down like that."],["Kaidan","There's only one possibility. There's a <yellow>traitor</yellow> at this dock..."],["","Harvey glanced at Kaidan's expression—eyes firm, mouth tight, there was no doubt he was serious."],["Harvey","Kaidan, calm down."],["Harvey","Ann is a bit eccentric, that's true, but she doesn't seem like a spy, does she?"],["Kaidan","Then let's go through it from start to finish, one by one."],["Kaidan","First, we can rule out everyone from GKD Parcel Service. Each of us is a well-known, vested partner... No one would stab themselves in the back."],["Kaidan","Next, there's the Electric Eel duo... These two weren't originally part of this game, they ended up here by chance."],["Kaidan","Even if they had the motive, they don't have the capability. They're notorious and have a record of collaborating with the NDF... The DL wouldn't trust them."],["Kaidan","In which case, we're left with just one person..."],["","Hearing Kaidan say this, Harvey also began to feel a bit puzzled. She paused slightly and started to seriously recall her past experiences with Ann."],["Harvey","...What kind of spy would be so easily tricked? They were suckered by the ads, cheated out of all their money."],["Harvey","Even if the Defense Forces were short-staffed, they wouldn't pick someone this reckless, would they?"],["Kaidan","What you see as recklessness may just be an act. A so-called newcomer to the island—it could just be a way to cover up her past."],["Kaidan","Harvey, think carefully, isn't all this trouble caused by her?"],["Harvey","......"],["Kaidan","You stored so many STs in the hangar, who precisely picked out that \"Nephthys\"?"],["Kaidan","Who, after getting the ST, didn't even warm the cockpit before charging straight into the Defense Force's encirclement?"],["Kaidan","And who, just after being taken to the dock, turned around and left, leaving the Defense Force to surround this place completely?"],["Kaidan","I don't want to sound too harsh, but the fact is... wherever she goes, the Defense Force follows."],["","After this conversation, Harvey pretty much understood her companion's thoughts... She sighed and synchronized the tracked information to Kaidan."],["Harvey","Since you put it that way, it would be rather impolite for me to stop you."],["Harvey","Here, this is her location."],["Harvey","She's... with those Electric Eel people."],["Kaidan","So, that's the situation."],["Kaidan","Do you understand now? You can relax, this has nothing to do with you two."],["Kaidan","Cooperate, and I won't make things difficult for you."],["","That being said, even after Kaidan finished explaining, Movme and Fenrir still stood blocking the way, showing no sign of backing down."],["Movme","...And what if this old man says no?!"],["Movme","Sorry, but this girl is now a member of the Super Electric Eels!"],["Movme","Spy? Mole? If GKD's got an intel leak, that's your problem! Don't try to pin it on us!"],["","After speaking, Movme instead adopted a provocative expression and stepped forward."],["Kaidan","Interesting... Standing up for a newcomer you've known for less than a day."],["Kaidan","Electric Eels, being so loyal? Are you guys feeling okay? What's going on?"],["Fenrir","Loyalty? Who cares about such boring things... I just can't stand the way you throw your weight around!"],["Fenrir","Before, you tied us up with the excuse of preventing leaks, and now that the military goods have been taken back by the Defense Force, you're blaming us again?"],["Fenrir","What's the matter? Are we some kind of punching bag for you to vent on whenever things don't go your way?"],["","Seeing that neither of them had any intention of cooperating, Kaidan began to lose patience."],["Kaidan","So... you've set your mind on going against the GKD?"],["Kaidan","You may not like us, and I know scheming is in your nature. But I'll give you one last friendly warning: Do not do anything stupid."],["Kaidan","Don't mistake this reckless urge for courage."],["Kaidan","This has nothing to do with you. Hand over the girl named Ann, and this will all end here."],["Fenrir","Then let me remind you..."],["Fenrir","We're the Super Electric Eels... Don't look down on us!"],["","The bullet grazed past Kaidan—this was Electric Eel's final response to the negotiation."],["Movme","Did you get something wrong? I've already told you, Ann is now with the Super Electric Eels!"],["Movme","If you mess with her... you're messing with us!"],["Movme","In short, we're protecting this girl! If you have a grievance, go to the ST and find the DL—don't mess with us!"],["","Kaidan wasn't too surprised, but he waved his hand regretfully."],["Kaidan","Alright, alright, I knew it wouldn't be easy, but... I didn't expect you to be quite this stubborn."],["Kaidan","Well, I guess I could use a warm-up."],["","In an instant, Kaidan's gaze turned cold."],["","In the span of a breath, he stormed through Electric Eel's encirclement, charging like a leopard on the hunt."],["Fenrir","Stay alert! He's coming!"]],"560328301":[["","And so, the fight finally came to an end with Ann's accidental friendly fire."],["","After being brought out, Ann thought she would face a brutal interrogation... But unexpectedly, Kaidan didn't make things too difficult for her."],["","Instead, they openly invited both her and Electric Eel to their temporary camp."],["Movme","Wh-what do you mean by this? You're not planning to interrogate us together, are you?!"],["Movme","Let me tell you, no matter what tricks you play, Movme never yields! Even when the boss's bat hit my head before, I never cried out in pain!"],["Kaidan","No, I've changed my mind... This young girl probably isn't a mole."],["Ann","Eh, eh—Really?!"],["Fenrir","Oh? Did it really take a huge brawl for you to finally listen?"],["Kaidan","Do you know... how the Defense Force trains undercover agents?"],["Fenrir","Who knows about such things... It's probably through coercion, bribery, and winning hearts and minds."],["Kaidan","No, those can at best be considered \"informants.\" For those who truly hold confidential information... they'd never be so careless."],["Kaidan","Milkhama Island has a large number of war-orphaned children who have long been cut off from society and have no one to rely on. Raising them is as simple as drawing on a blank sheet of paper."],["Kaidan","They raise these children, train them intensively in these so-called \"schools,\" assign them new identities, teach them how to deceive, how to survive, how to kill, how to... betray."],["Fenrir","You suspect... that girl is one of them?"],["Fenrir","But if they're really as mysterious as you say, what's made you change your mind?"],["Kaidan","These people carry a certain strength—or perhaps a flaw. Just as handling a gun leaves calluses, those who've undergone that kind of all-round training develop an instinct to fight back the moment their life is threatened."],["Kaidan","And that girl... she's like a babe in the woods, showing no sense of danger even when facing death."],["Kaidan","This impression of complete defenselessness, even the best spies can't perform it convincingly."],["Fenrir","I'm starting to get curious, where did you hear all this from?"],["Kaidan","A... friend. You wouldn't want to know the details."],["Ann","From what you're saying, it seems the mole is someone else, right? It can't be anything to do with me, can it?"],["Ann","So can you let me go? As for that ST... let's just forget about it."],["Kaidan","Not really, the problem still seems to be with you."],["Kaidan","Dana, search her."],["","Before Ann could react, Dana had already made her move, stumbling forward to firmly Control the opponent."],["Ann","Huh—"],["Dana","Relax, it will be over soon."],["","Dana's fingers swiftly swept over the opponent, not intending to miss a single pocket or concealed spot."],["Dana","Finally, her fingers stopped at Ann's back, where a strange indentation caught her attention."],["Ann","Ouch, that really stings..."],["Dana","Subdermal implants? The Defense Force just keeps sinking to new lows."],["Dana","Hold on, this might hurt a little."],["Ann","Wait, I'm not ready... Agh!"],["","Dana tightly grasped the piece of skin with one hand, and in an instant, completed the incision with the other... Precise, swift—just as a sniper should be."],["","Before Ann could make a sound, the foreign object under the skin had already been removed, even flashing a faint indicator light."],["Dana","It's this locator that betrayed our whereabouts."],["Dana","I've dealt with the outer device, but the internal chip is buried too deep... I'll have to leave it for now."],["Ann","Phew, so the misunderstanding's resolved. Now, with that settled, what say we go our separate ways?"],["Kaidan","No, I went to great lengths to clear your name, not just to let you walk away."],["Kaidan","I have a proposal—maybe we can try working together."],["Ann","Work together... What?!"]],"560329101":[["","Meanwhile, DL Military Base..."],["DLAF Deputy","Lieutenant, the convoy has successfully completed the transfer mission of \"Nephthys.\" No resistance was encountered during transit."],["Victoria","Hmph, they ended up being useful after all."],["Victoria","We're not done. Move the escort units to the defense line right away, and double the manpower at each key position."],["DLAF Deputy","But, sir..."],["DLAF Deputy","Officer Ma'at just sent word that Councilor Lukmund urgently requested you to pull back and immediately dispatch reinforcements to his sector."],["Victoria","This is a critical moment; it's impossible to reshuffle our forces now."],["Victoria","Tell him... The situation is urgent. We cannot comply."],["Victoria","Before the DL forces officially receive this \"Nephthys,\" I will not allow any of you to let your guard down!"],["DLAF Deputy","But sir, Officer Ma'at has already redirected the outer mobile units through the command system."],["DLAF Deputy","Our manpower... is already insufficient."],["Victoria","Damn it, why now?!"],["DLAF Deputy","Lieutenant, do we really... need to go this far?"],["DLAF Deputy","They're just a mercenary group. At this point, I don't think they have the ability to resist anymore."],["","After speaking, the adjutant closed his eyes, waiting for a harsh scolding."],["","Unexpectedly, Victoria just gave him a cold glare."],["Victoria","Adjutant, have you ever seen those leopards on the grasslands?"],["Victoria","These beasts are neither as fierce as lions nor as robust as giant bears. They survive by relying on another set of qualities—cunning and paranoia."],["Victoria","Once they set their sights on prey, they never give up, but instead shadow their target closely... In the moment their prey relaxes, they reveal their claws and bite through the throat."],["DLAF Deputy","So, GKD Parcel Service hasn't given up yet?"],["DLAF Deputy","Indeed, we set up so many sentry posts before, and haven't caught a glimpse of them. The tracker you placed on that hidden asset has also lost signal..."],["","*beep-beep-beep*"],["","As if responding to the adjutant's inner unease, the communication channel that had been silent for a long time suddenly started to sound alarms."],["DL Soldier","Officer! Several STs are approaching the base."],["DL Soldier","The frontline units have already engaged them... Confirmed: It's the GKD Squad!"],["DLAF Deputy","What?!"],["Victoria","So they finally showed up, eh?"],["Victoria","Adjutant, get the boys in camp on their feet... Deploy according to my previous action plan."],["DLAF Deputy","That suppression operation? But with our current forces, I'm afraid we can't maintain the encirclement!"],["Victoria","Then mobilize the base garrison as well. I want every position filled, down to the man! Not a single gap will be tolerated!"],["DLAF Deputy","But if we do that, the base's defense will..."],["Victoria","You've tangled with GKD Parcel Service before, so you should be well aware of their capabilities. They excel at dragging things out and tying you down; to beat them, you must leave them no chance to resist."],["Victoria","Or do you want the previous failure to repeat?"],["DLAF Deputy","No, sir... I'll start preparing immediately."],["Victoria","Any destabilizing factors threatening the DL should not exist."],["Victoria","GKD, this is the end for you."],["","The pursuit was more intense than either side had anticipated."],["","STs from both sides fought from outside the camp to the docks, turning the entire coastline into a battlefield."],["","The GKD Squad launched several raids, at one point even tearing through the Defense Force's line, pushing directly to the center of their formation."],["","But under Victoria's command, the Defense Force soldiers displayed unusual tenacity, rallying after each blow and quickly filling the gaps."],["","The battle thus reached a stalemate."],["Kaidan","Ha, I thought you looked familiar. You're the commander from the Central Mining Area, aren't you?"],["Kaidan","I've heard about you. That lone eagle of the Defense Force, always decisive, always one step ahead... After two encounters, I can see it's true."],["Victoria","Don't try to get close to me, GKD rats! I let you go last time, but this time... I'm not feeling so generous."],["Kaidan","Oh? Don't get ahead of yourself. Your side hasn't gained the advantage yet."],["Victoria","Really? Then why don't you ask your sniper how many bullets are left in her magazine?"],["Victoria","Or talk to your machinist friend there and see how long the armor on his ST can last?"],["Kaidan","......"],["Kaidan","...Interesting. You sure have an eye for detail."],["Victoria","GKD Parcel Service, I'll admit, you have some skills. Going toe-to-toe with the DL's finest is no small feat."],["Victoria","——But in the end, you just can't win!"],["Victoria","How do I put this? You're like a sharp blade, a fearsome weapon indeed... But it takes more than one weapon to beat an army."],["","Despite Victoria's threats and aggression, Kaidan showed no sign of panic, as if he had already anticipated her reaction."],["Kaidan","Well, that's hard to say."],["Kaidan","Is it possible... that from the very beginning, we never intended to win?"],["Victoria","...Nonsense!"],["","Just as Victoria raised her weapon, preparing to order the soldiers to launch the next wave of attacks, an urgent call suddenly came through."],["DL Soldier","Command, do you read? Command, come in!"],["DL Soldier","The base is under attack by unknown assailants. They've breached the outpost and penetrated inside!"],["DL Soldier","We're short on manpower... can't hold out much longer!"],["DL Soldier","Repeat—Command, come in! The base is under attack, requesting immediate support!"],["Kaidan","Looks like we made it in time."],["Victoria","What's the meaning of this?! Where did these troops come from?"],["","Victoria clenched her teeth. Clearly, such a turn of events was beyond her expectations."],["Victoria","I've gone through all your battle records. Everyone from GKD Parcel Service... should have been caught on this battlefield!"],["Kaidan","Lieutenant, your preparations were thorough, but you overlooked one crucial thing—from the very beginning, your opponents were not just the GKD."],["Kaidan","The ones attacking your headquarters are some... minor characters you didn't even consider."],["Victoria","...Damn it!"],["","Victoria's fist angrily slammed onto the console, she gritted her teeth and lifted her head, staring intently at the enemy that was so close."],["Victoria","Don't think these little tricks will save you... I'll crush you first, then deal with the mess over there!"],["","No sooner had she spoken than a burst of gunfire poured out at Victoria's command."],["","But Kaidan seemed to have anticipated it; using the nearby cover, he easily neutralized the Defense Force's fierce assault."],["Kaidan","Lieutenant, losing your cool already?"],["Kaidan","You carefully calculated our remaining ammo and logistics, didn't you? Then you should know exactly how long we can hold out..."],["Kaidan","Your strategic target isn't GKD Parcel Service, is it? Is it really okay to let the hard-earned ST be taken away like this?"],["Victoria","You...!"],["","Victoria clenched her teeth tightly, anger burning in her eyes. She trembled, on the verge of exploding."],["Victoria","Lieutenant, listen to my orders..."],["","But no matter how indignant she was, she couldn't deny it... He was right."],["Victoria","I'll take the first and third squads back. You'll have full command over the rest of the troops."],["DLAF Deputy","Lieutenant, are we really going to let them go like this?!"],["Victoria","Shut up and listen quietly!"],["Victoria","I don't expect you to defeat them... just hold them off for me!"],["DLAF Deputy","Understood... I'll delay them as much as possible for you."],["Victoria","One more thing... Adjutant, tell me, who exactly attacked the base?!"],["DLAF Deputy","It was a group of... illegal mercenaries. They rejected any communication initiated by us and launched an attack as soon as they entered the base's perimeter."],["DLAF Deputy","These people call themselves the \"Super Electric Eels.\" I once arrested them at the border and detained them in the experiment area..."],["DLAF Deputy","They escaped our control during that chaos. I thought they were just ordinary fugitives. I would never have expected..."],["Fenrir","Still talking about cooperation even now?"],["Fenrir","Sorry, but I refuse... For all we know, you're just looking for cannon fodder."],["Movme","Same here! After everything you did to us? You must be joking! I haven't even begun to settle the score with you!"],["Movme","Do you think a few words can wipe the slate clean? Dream on! I'd rather starve than cooperate with you scumbags!"],["Kaidan","Ha, I thought after all these years of crawling and fighting on the battlefield, you'd still have some backbone left."],["Kaidan","The Electric Eel I knew would never look so defeated... Electric Eel, scared of the DLAF? What's going on?"],["Fenrir","...That isn't going to work."],["Fenrir","We are now the Super Electric Eels, free mercenaries living for ourselves."],["Fenrir","Such intangible things can't fool us. If you want us to take action... make a real offer!"],["","Upon hearing Fenrir's retort, Kaidan merely smiled slightly—he seemed to have anticipated this response."],["Kaidan","How about helping you <yellow>make a name for yourselves</yellow>?"],["Fenrir","Huh? What do you mean?!"],["Kaidan","I've heard about the things you've been through. Heard it from Harvey and that Ann girl."],["Kaidan","First, you was turned away from West Island, then caught by the Defense Force patrol and thrown into prison to be used as human test subjects..."],["Kaidan","And what about those high and mighty types, those who look down on you? Don't you want to show them a thing or two?"],["Fenrir","......"],["Movme","Of course I do! The way those guys look at us, it's like we're dogs... I still can't forget it!"],["Ann","But... can we really handle them on our own? Even as a newcomer, I know those regular troops were no pushovers..."],["Kaidan","What do you have in mind?"],["Kaidan","Next, we will launch an attack on the main battlefield. Given the straightforward temperament of the opposing commander, she'll likely gather her main force to confront us..."],["Kaidan","...leaving her main base mostly vacant. The base that houses that \"Nephthys\"."],["Fenrir","Hit their base head on while they're distracted, huh...?"],["Kaidan","That's it. Think about it, what kind of business do the mercenaries on this island do? It's nothing more than petty theft, bullying, doing the jobs that the regular army wouldn't stoop to do."],["Kaidan","There are these mercs, a group of psychos called the \"Super Electric Eels\"..."],["Kaidan","They hate small-time combat, preferring to hit the DL right where it hurts, braving the fire of the Defense Forces to wreak havoc far behind their lines..."],["Kaidan","Could anything help you gain a <yellow>reputation</yellow> faster than this?"],["Fenrir","......"],["Movme","......"],["","Both Fenrir and Movme fell silent."],["","But Kaidan showed no sign of impatience... He knew very well that the answer was already in their hearts."],["Movme","Fenrir, I think there's a chance... What do you think?"],["Fenrir","Hmph... I have only one question."],["Fenrir","Kaidan, your target is that \"Nephthys,\" right? Aren't you afraid... that while we're causing trouble, we'll end up hijacking your precious ST as well?"],["Kaidan","No, after all... this thing is useless to you. You wouldn't want to hold onto this hot potato, would you?"],["Fenrir","GKD Parcel Service... You really have us completely figured out."],["Fenrir","Let's not waste time, let's get to the nitty-gritty. We're taking this job."]],"560329301":[["","As Lieutenant Victoria predicted, all I can do is... buy time."],["","The encirclement, lacking manpower, leaks like a sieve. Despite the adjutant's desperate efforts, it ultimately fails to stop the GKD's advance."],["","When the adjutant returned to the camp with the troops... it was already too late."],["","Their officer was kneeling silently in front of the ruins."],["","Despite being severely damaged, the adjutant immediately recognized... this is the ST \"Nephthys,\" the one they were meant to protect."],["Victoria","......"],["DLAF Deputy","Officer Victoria, are you... alright...?"],["Victoria","Pursue..."],["DLAF Deputy","...Pursue?"],["Victoria","Adjutant, immediately assemble our available forces and contact all the patrols on the perimeter..."],["Victoria","Pursue the GKD Squad! Even if they flee to the ends of the earth, under no circumstances must you let them escape!"],["DLAF Deputy","......"],["Victoria","Lieutenant, why aren't you getting ready to depart?! Are you going to defy my orders like those other weak soldiers?!"],["","The composure and demeanor of a commander have vanished... Now, all that remains in Victoria is the bitterness of failure and helpless anger."],["","Just as Victoria drew her pistol and aimed it at the lieutenant, the communicator at her waist rang."],["Ma'at","Enough, Lieutenant Victoria."],["Ma'at","\"Nephthys\" no longer holds any value for further research and testing. Your mission—has failed."],["Victoria","Ma'at! You have no right to accuse me!"],["Victoria","If it weren't for you pulling my troops halfway through, this would never have happened!"],["Victoria","It's not over yet! Even with just these troops at hand, I will definitely... find GKD Parcel Service!"],["Ma'at","......"],["Ma'at","Lieutenant Victoria, Lord Lukmund often mentions you. He says... he admires you."],["Ma'at","Because you are different from other defense forces, not the kind who, when something goes wrong, tries to find excuses to shirk responsibility."],["Victoria","...!"],["Ma'at","Lieutenant, you're not an unreasonable person. You should be well aware that there's no need for this battle to continue."],["Ma'at","Continuing to bet will only make your defeat, no, I should say the DL's defeat... even more devastating."],["","Pain, humiliation, anger. This is not the first time Victoria has tasted such feelings."],["","Like the look in my father's eyes when he witnessed the \"Apocalypse\"... like the silhouette of the sand whale as it departed... so bitter, so regretful."],["","After a long silence, she finally... swallowed this unwillingness."],["Victoria","I... understand..."],["Victoria","I will cease combat immediately... deploy according to your instructions and head to the western front."],["Ma'at","Lieutenant, I'm glad to see you're still composed."],["Ma'at","Out of goodwill, I'll remind you once more—Lieutenant, your recent actions are enough to land you in a military court."],["Ma'at","If you want to continue serving in the Defense Force, then you'd better remember your place... Don't let Lord Lukmund down again."],["","As the transmission ends, the air is once again filled with suffocating silence. Even though the conversation is over, Victoria remains standing, clutching the communicator tightly."],["","...until the adjutant's footsteps broke the somber atmosphere."],["DLAF Deputy","Lieutenant, the remaining troops have been rallied."],["DLAF Deputy","All soldiers present, follow the lieutenant's instructions... As soon as you give the order, we can strike at any time!"],["Victoria","Clean up the aftermath and let the soldiers rest well... In an hour, we will move to the battlefield on the west side."],["DLAF Deputy","But officer, what about the GKD...?"],["Victoria","Adjutant, didn't you hear the transmission just now?"],["DLAF Deputy","......"],["Victoria","Then don't argue—follow Ma'at's instructions!"],["Victoria","As the Defense Force, executing orders is our top priority. Besides... we'll get our revenge eventually."],["DLAF Deputy","Understood, Lieutenant..."],["","The adjutant nodded and silently withdrew."],["","Furious, teeth clenched... after all this, her eyes were left with only cold anger and hatred."],["Victoria","Kaidan Newman, and everyone at GKD Parcel Service... I've memorized all your names and faces."],["Victoria","In the battle at the Central Mining Area, you escaped thanks to those traitors. This time, it's due to my misjudgment and those short-sighted bureaucrats... But luck won't always favor you!"],["Victoria","And those two clowns you call themselves Super Electric Eels... The same goes for them."],["Victoria","We will meet again on the battlefield. I will find you, crush you, and savor your dying screams."],["Victoria","Just wait for me. I will make you pay for your arrogance!"],["Movme","Ah—choo!"],["Movme","Damn allergies, I was just getting into it!"],["Fenrir","All this guy does is blow hot air..."],["Fenrir","Alright, let's continue—"],["Fenrir","In the blink of an eye, facing the encirclement of the defense forces, I pulled the control lever and executed a slide tackle!"],["","After the dust settled, Fenrir and Movme took advantage of the GKD Parcel Service's cover to slip back into UNCS territory."],["","With nothing to do, the two returned to the familiar bar, but this time, as the \"Super Electric Eels.\""],["Mercenary","So according to you, you guys got caught by the Defense Forces... on purpose. All so you could make a daring escape?"],["Mercenary","Hahaha, you two are full of it, do you really think we've never encountered the DL regulars?!"],["Fenrir","Heh, I knew someone would say that."],["","Fenrir didn't rush to refute the other party, but instead pointed to the screen over the merc's head."],["","Movme and Fenrir's mugshots are prominently displayed on the wanted poster issued by the DL, with charges such as \"Destruction of Military Facilities\" and \"Illegal Infiltration of Military Zones\" specially noted."],["Fenrir","Can you read? Or do you need me to read it for you?"],["Fenrir","We are now officially certified fugitives according to the Defense Forces."],["Mercenary","Tch, who would believe that! You must be pulling something."],["Movme","Not convinced? Then go ahead and challenge them yourself. The Foren River is right over there—go on! Or are you just all talk?!"],["Mercenary","Have you had enough of pretending? Don't think I don't know that without Frida, you wouldn't get many jobs. You're just living off the name of the old captain Warren, who's been dead for years! Maybe some people will be fooled by you, but I won't!"],["Mercenary","Just a couple of good-for-nothing punks, washed-up mercs their old boss kicked to the curb! Now you think you're all tough, calling yourselves the \"Super Electric Eels\"? What a joke! You'd better..."],["Mercenary","Gah—!!"],["","Before the mercenary could finish speaking, Movme had already jumped up from his chair and dunked the other's head directly into the basin."],["Movme","Say that again, I dare you! I never ride on anyone's coattails! Fenrir on the other hand... anyway, what's it to you?!"],["Mercenary","You bastard... Are you looking for a fight?!"],["Movme","Bring it on, I've never been afraid of anyone!"],["","Two things draw the attention of mercs: money and mayhem. The nearby patrons put down their drinks, stirred by the commotion. As the atmosphere thickened, Fenrir's anger boiled over—he struck the table and sprang to his feet."],["Onlooking Mercenary","Hahaha, this'll be quite the spectacle!"],["Jeering Mercenary","Fight! Fight!"],["","Amidst the commotion, no one noticed a pitch-black figure entering the shop."],["","That's enough!"],["","Just as emotions reached their peak and both sides were about to come to blows, a heavy thud of a bat hitting the floor suddenly echoed from the entrance."],["","It wasn't loud, yet it carried a familiar aura... An undeniable authority."],["Frida","You've got some nerve causing trouble on Electric Eel's turf."],["","With Frida's appearance, the schadenfreude of the onlookers and the boiling tension of the crowd vanished instantly. They returned to their tables in silence."],["","The master of Electric Eel didn't leave but instead took a seat at the table where the argument had just occurred—Fenrir and Movme's table."],["Movme","B-boss..."],["Fenrir","Frida, how come you're here?"],["","Frida ignored their hostility and instead raised her glass, confidently downing her drink in one go."],["Frida","So what, now you're rich and famous, you're too good to see your old boss?"],["Fenrir","Hmph, if you're here to laugh at us... I advise you to save it."],["Frida","Easy now. We've charged into danger together more than a few times... I have no doubt you pulled off something big in the east."],["Frida","I came here because I want to talk about cooperating on something."],["Fenrir","Cooperating?! You have the nerve to mention that word?"],["Frida","Well, let's see. After going solo for so long, you should have realized by now—even a leaky boat beats being left to swim the open sea."],["Frida","Mercenaries are not just about fighting; they need to know how to expand the business and how to let everyone... taste the benefits."],["Frida","In Electric Eel, I've always kept two spots for you. I can assure you, once you return, no one will ever speak ill of you again."],["","Faced with Frida's generous invitation, Fenrir was somewhat moved."],["","As if to dispel his inner hesitation, he shook his head and returned to the cold, grinning expression he had earlier."],["Fenrir","Frida, I'm really sorry... it's already too late."],["Fenrir","We are now the Super Electric Eels, an independent mercenary group that stands on its own. Don't treat us like your underlings."],["Movme","That's right! Life may be tough here, but we enjoy our freedom... Now, I can fight whoever I want, without all the rules we had in Electric Eel!"],["Movme","Boss, I used to really respect you—no, to be fair, I still think you're a decent person. But I really have to say this... You're stuck in the past!"],["","Frida raised her eyebrows slightly, maintaining a confident smile, seemingly not surprised by their response."],["Frida","Heh... You've grown more independent... ambitious as well."],["Frida","Since you're now your own mercenary group, let's change the way we cooperate."],["Frida","Are you interested... in becoming shareholders of Electric Eel?"],["Fenrir","Frida, what do you mean by that?"],["Frida","Shareholder, second-in-command, third-in-command, supervisor, manager, whatever... It's all the same to me."],["Frida","No more groveling before middlemen, no more borrowing other people's names to network, bluff, swindle... The way it is now, you nod, we give our approval, and you're a legit partner of Electric Eel."],["Frida","No more worrying about who came first, no longer just henchmen, but elite mercenaries sharing profits and losses with all of Electric Eel... From now on, the benefits of Electric Eel are your benefits. The reputation of Electric Eel is your reputation."],["Movme","Oh! So that means we'd be able to throw our weight around like the boss... hold on, you know about all that? Let me just say this: that was all Fenrir's bragging and—mmmph!"],["Fenrir","Hey Movme, look, your favorite fried chicken—eat up! Ahem, Frida, let's not talk about the past now! I just want to know, why did you suddenly agree to... such a high price?"],["Frida","Times have changed, and you've proven your strength, so of course I have some good faith."],["Frida","This island is about to undergo a transformation... In the new era, there will be a place for you."],["Frida","I heard you took in a new recruit. I haven't seen them yet."],["Fenrir","You mean Ann?"],["Fenrir","Oh, she bought some military equipment from Harvey, and then accidentally blew it up. She owes GKD a pretty enormous debt."],["Fenrir","GKD Parcel Service asked us for people, so we might as well do them a favor and kick this little girl out... No tagalongs, that's what you taught us."],["Movme","Wait, that's not what you said back then."],["Movme","When we left, I remember you were muttering to yourself—something like \"We're already stuck here with no way out, can't drag others down\"... You even told Kaidan to take care of her!"],["Fenrir","Can't you eat a little more and talk a little less?!"],["Fenrir","Let's change the subject... If we become shareholders of Electric Eel, what in it for us precisely...?"],["","Thus, Movme and Fenrir once again reconciled with Frida, rejoining as shareholders."],["","What neither of them realizes yet is that \"sharing the profits\" comes with \"sharing the losses\"..."],["","Many years later, whenever they repay the debts incurred by Electric Eel, they always remember that afternoon when they raised their glasses and swore an oath with Frida."],["","*cough, cough... cough cough cough...*"],["","Ann, don't cry. You've grown up and no longer need Grandpa's stories."],["","Sigh, you're saying those willful things again."],["","You want to be a gold miner like Grandpa, but do you know the fate of us gold miners?"],["","......"],["","Forget it, some stories are better left without an ending. Besides... even if I tell you, you'll still go to that island."],["","It's a pity that besides this shovel, Grandpa has nothing else to leave you."],["","Hehe, then take it with you, just as you wished... Set foot on this island as a gold miner."],["Ann","......"],["Ann","When I was a child, every time I asked Grandpa if he wanted to go back to the mine, he always said he could never return to this island."],["Ann","But now... I think I'm starting to understand."],["Ann","It's not that there's no ship to return on, but this island... is vastly different from the island of my grandpa's time."],["","Thinking of this, she couldn't help but grip the shovel in her hand."],["Ann","But Grandpa, if they were true gold miners... they wouldn't care what this island has become."],["Ann","You said that bad things are inevitable, and good things cannot be forced. For gold miners, what truly matters... is that they are on the journey."],["Ann","You and the gold miners... won't be the end of this story. I will keep going until I find my treasure, even my path winds on and on..."],["Harvey","Ann, what are you daydreaming about over there!"],["Ann","Uh... j-just... thinking about some old stuff..."],["Harvey","Today's work has already started. Come on, there's no time for that."],["Harvey","Ahem, let me say it again. Accessories and ammo must be stored separately, and each mech should be categorized according to type and purpose. This way, when you need them, you can achieve twice the result with half the effort."],["Harvey","Also, the STs on display need regular dusting to maintain a fresh look and give those customers a good impression."],["Harvey","Do you understand?"],["Ann","Got it, got it! Accessories should be placed in Area A of the hangar, while ammo goes in Area B... Hold on, I'll start the dryer right away to dehumidify them!"],["Harvey","Hey, wait! You can't just turn it on, it will..."],["","When Harvey noticed the accessories tumbling in the drum, it was already too late."],["","As the heat took hold, the metal casings and the powder inside the bullets began to warp. The intense shock of the high heat and pressure caused the dryer to buckle like a deflated ball before it went up in a massive, roaring explosion."],["Ann","Ahaha, looks like I messed up..."],["Harvey","*cough*... You! Go mop the deck! I forbid you from appearing in the hangar again!"],["","Looking at the new scorch marks on the wall, Dana sighed helplessly."],["Dana","Kaidan, are you really planning to let her work with us?"],["Dana","This reckless girl... I'm really afraid she'll blow up our safe house one day."],["Kaidan","Don't look at me, if you want to blame someone... blame our dear captain."],["Kaidan","In the end, it's all because she just happened to choose such a \"premium customer.\""],["Kaidan","Now Nephthys has been half-destroyed by the Defense Force's artillery, leaving us with nothing but some superficial data... Oh, and Ann's IOU."],["Dana","Can't you persuade Harvey to just write it off?"],["Dana","She's shrewd enough—I'm sure she can make back that loss if she just picks up a few extra jobs, don't you think?"],["Grant","I don't think that's going to cut it, I'm afraid."],["Grant","This little girl has more creditors than just Harvey; she's racked up quite a bit of debt along the way..."],["Grant","Brokerage fees, ammo fees, maintenance fees, oh, she even pawned that ST to open a Harpy Platinum Membership... By the end of this trip, the interest has skyrocketed."],["Grant","If we want to write it off, we'll have to pay her instead!"],["Kaidan","In any case... that's the situation. Dana, if you get the chance, teach her a thing or two."],["Dana","You're spoiling her too much, Kaidan."],["","Dana shook her head and decided not to look at the pair of jokers in the hangar anymore, turning back to calibrating her scope."],["Grant","So... does that mean the little girl is officially a member of GKD Parcel Service?"],["Kaidan","Yes, we've lost the opportunity to delve deeper into the Nephthys system, and it will likely be quite some time before we find a similar technological sample."],["Kaidan","The only clue related to those technologies is the chip implanted in Ann by the Defense Force..."],["Kaidan","But, putting these factors aside... are you really going to throw an inexperienced newcomer straight to the wolves?"],["Grant","Well, well... it's rare to see the boss this sentimental. What, does she remind you of yourself when you first arrived on the island?"],["Kaidan","Are you kidding? If I were like her, I would have been taken down by the puppets you created back in the NDF."],["Kaidan","I was just thinking... how did this island go from being a symbol of freedom and wealth to what it is now?"],["Kaidan","War, hate, greed... it's like an invisible vortex, pulling everyone in without them even realizing."],["Kaidan","Whether by force or by choice, times like these have taken people far from their original paths, much like the island."],["Grant","Ha, if everyone were as pure as this little girl, the island would have been peaceful long ago."],["Grant","But boss, you know very well... It's beyond our control. There's no point thinking about it."],["Kaidan","That's right, all we can do is give her this opportunity."],["Kaidan","This island can accommodate so much ambition, so much madness—one more gold miner shouldn't be a problem."],["Kaidan","Let Ann truly understand the real face of Milkhama Island while working to pay off her debts."],["Kaidan","As for whether to stay or leave in the end... I believe she will have an answer by then."],["Grant","It seems that our place is going to get lively again."],["","As the sun sets, the outline of the Deserted Island slowly fades away with the arrival of dusk."],["","Some see it as a paradise, some view it as a battlefield; some treat it as an experimental field, some regard it as a grave; and for some... it's their only remaining home."],["","But regardless of their mindset, everyone understands that dusk will pass, night will fall, and this island will once again welcome a long darkness."],["","...But what comes after the darkness?"],["","There has to be a spark, something that lets people remember, even standing amidst the ruins, the island's original nature."]]};
